"https://api.github.com/users/soc221b/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/soc221b/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/soc221b","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-env/import-meta-env/commits/dfff222a56c31169ace90e067cdbf5c10a6c401f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-12T05:32:14Z","email":"soc221b.e@gmail.com","name":"Ernest"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-12T05:32:14Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(examples): regenerate webpack-module-federation-example package-lock.json (#2273)\n\n### Motivation\n- `npm ci` in the webpack module federation example failed because the\nlockfile was out of sync and missing optional peer dependency artifacts\n(`encoding@0.1.13` and nested `iconv-lite@0.6.3`), preventing clean CI\ninstalls.\n- Regenerate the example''s lockfile to align transitive resolutions so\ndeterministic installs work with `npm ci`.\n\n### Description\n- Regenerated\n`packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example/package-lock.json`\nby running `npm install` in the example directory, which updated many\ntransitive dependency entries and versions.\n- The updated lockfile now includes `encoding@0.1.13` and the nested\n`encoding/node_modules/iconv-lite@0.6.3` entries required by\n`node-fetch`''s optional peer dependency.\n- Committed the regenerated lockfile with the Angular-style message\n`chore(examples): regenerate webpack module federation lockfile`.\n\n### Testing\n- Ran `npm install` in\n`packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example` and it completed\nsuccessfully.\n- Ran `npm ci` in `packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example`\nand it completed successfully.\n- Verified presence of the lockfile entries with `node -e \"const\nl=require(''./packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example/package-lock.json'');\nconsole.log(!!l.packages[''node_modules/encoding''],\n!!l.packages[''node_modules/iconv-lite'']);\"` which returned both `true`.\n\n------\n[Codex\nTask](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/tasks/task_e_69db27acac5c832391d98f63807ce96d)","tree":{"sha":"ed37c071ecfc593506d84c77f1812c700fe4da17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-env/import-meta-env/git/trees/ed37c071ecfc593506d84c77f1812c700fe4da17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-env/import-meta-env/git/commits/dfff222a56c31169ace90e067cdbf5c10a6c401f","verification":{"payload":"tree ed37c071ecfc593506d84c77f1812c700fe4da17\nparent 15e8973a7a43f6b0a5de62a74280bd75b863d7f5\nauthor Ernest <soc221b.e@gmail.com> 1775971934 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1775971934 +0800\n\nchore(examples): regenerate webpack-module-federation-example package-lock.json (#2273)\n\n### Motivation\n- `npm ci` in the webpack module federation example failed because the\nlockfile was out of sync and missing optional peer dependency artifacts\n(`encoding@0.1.13` and nested `iconv-lite@0.6.3`), preventing clean CI\ninstalls.\n- Regenerate the example''s lockfile to align transitive resolutions so\ndeterministic installs work with `npm ci`.\n\n### Description\n- Regenerated\n`packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example/package-lock.json`\nby running `npm install` in the example directory, which updated many\ntransitive dependency entries and versions.\n- The updated lockfile now includes `encoding@0.1.13` and the nested\n`encoding/node_modules/iconv-lite@0.6.3` entries required by\n`node-fetch`''s optional peer dependency.\n- Committed the regenerated lockfile with the Angular-style message\n`chore(examples): regenerate webpack module federation lockfile`.\n\n### Testing\n- Ran `npm install` in\n`packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example` and it completed\nsuccessfully.\n- Ran `npm ci` in `packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example`\nand it completed successfully.\n- Verified presence of the lockfile entries with `node -e \"const\nl=require(''./packages/examples/webpack-module-federation-example/package-lock.json'');\nconsole.log(!!l.packages[''node_modules/encoding''],\n!!l.packages[''node_modules/iconv-lite'']);\"` which returned both `true`.\n\n------\n[Codex\nTask](https://chatgpt.com/codex/cloud/tasks/task_e_69db27acac5c832391d98f63807ce96d)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp2y5eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0+EQABgKLaLDmPdmwFVrcR1vJgQV\nR2Dsq8TM7jQQ6kvhDifWMb1FCMRVoSX+bkKB6UwJuK/S00gehYgam17oEsGrIafa\nmyNws05HSFA364Ps08ik9JwSEFGA0FRsBkRVuRmEQOtDHvvkn2DY/tid7Z9JhFLJ\nLj0JIsu6LY0j4I2SAwHwlm9Cl2PkHyKjYtujKoWNg1xIF3cdq7ErZNF2PAlio45J\nfHwzwaBncsypmiUqyU0WcOm0IskTYxwP2A2ia+YesfthF5dj+XAERn1gU4mQ+wD4\ntRXfAofaPygS2jTLJ4qhZFLkP00z0lXo05Dl92W/kvmnpcE9jqcUWvmRTwgkwIw4\nNqXDbASJgvA2K23xY0HuIQsOjGNuwABq+G8KyT2n2hL9E7A5ohnBuPIlLvo1i4Hh\nMZfpc4DotttvFhQobW3hGhkhMvZrwJmH5RlUeXpBV7MMOFW6lUiGx5UKon7KvoxC\nAmEeynvXSNbHtm3nTQ+pkNUQNUuD7K3Yg4H94DGR4cs95v4xPqZ4fUqKRsHOmGw8\n4CRkk4XP1Ucp3Hy4ept/tfSxD28X/Dja9svckFXYLks+eC/0dPfDh8WdU32mdZw5\nIeuVBevHGRQkIai3bEUXzfIkCi2N8XcpuzvaAY1aVUYxp3ZpsrHnps/TC4d/CCMn\nTj4HU1JS/CkfXs/REjRH\n=p9ka\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-12T05:32:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","s