tions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/renovate%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/runtime-env/import-meta-env/commits/319b592c22099eb0d4614f0217cb47bacd217c82/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-10-13T14:20:37Z","email":"29139614+renovate[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"renovate[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-13T14:20:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(deps): update dependency nuxt to v3.19.3 (#2226)\n\nThis PR contains the following updates:\n\n| Package | Change | Age | Confidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [nuxt](https://nuxt.com)\n([source](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/tree/HEAD/packages/nuxt))\n| [`3.16.2` ->\n`3.19.3`](https://renovatebot.com/diffs/npm/nuxt/3.16.2/3.19.3) |\n[![age](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/age/npm/nuxt/3.19.3?slim=true)](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/)\n|\n[![confidence](https://developer.mend.io/api/mc/badges/confidence/npm/nuxt/3.16.2/3.19.3?slim=true)](https://docs.renovatebot.com/merge-confidence/)\n|\n\n---\n\n### Release Notes\n\n<details>\n<summary>nuxt/nuxt (nuxt)</summary>\n\n###\n[`v3.19.3`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.19.3)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.19.2...v3.19.3)\n\n> **3.19.3** is a regularly scheduled patch release.\n\n#### ✅ Upgrading\n\nOur recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxt upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis will deduplicate your lockfile as well, and help ensure that you\npull in updates from other dependencies that Nuxt relies on,\nparticularly in the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.19.2...v3.19.3)\n\n##### 🔥 Performance\n\n- **vite:** Use rolldown''s replace plugin when applicable\n([#&#8203;33258](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33258))\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Make lazy component types compatible with `h`\n([#&#8203;33046](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33046))\n- **vite:** Deduplicate inlined server style chunks\n([#&#8203;33308](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33308))\n- **nuxt:** Support `head` option on `useHead`\n([#&#8203;33318](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33318))\n- **nuxt:** Do not relativise importmap if `cdnURL` is set\n([#&#8203;33333](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33333))\n- **nuxt:** Resolve aliases in `imports.dirs`\n([#&#8203;33334](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33334))\n- **nuxt:** Add missing element/vnode props for `<NuxtLink>`\n([#&#8203;33335](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33335))\n- **nuxt:** Do not generate server placeholder components\n([#&#8203;33345](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33345))\n- **nuxt:** Dedupe generated component names\n([#&#8203;33346](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33346))\n- **webpack:** Test watch instance before closing it\n([3314bc9a1](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/3314bc9a1))\n- **nuxt:** Correctly handle island rendering error\n([#&#8203;33302](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33302))\n- **nuxt:** Support `v-slot:fallback` longform syntax in `<DevOnly>`\n([#&#8203;33368](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33368))\n- **nuxt:** Support `typeFrom` when generating auto-import type\ntemplates\n([#&#8203;33373](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33373))\n- **nuxt:** Don''t trigger scroll when changing trailing slash\n([#&#8203;33358](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33358))\n- **nuxt:** Add stubs for new scripts from `@nuxt/scripts`\n([057ade490](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/057ade490))\n- **nuxt:** Prevent duplicate execution on key change in `useAsyncData`\n([#&#8203;33325](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33325))\n- **nuxt:** Make middleware `_path` property configurable for HMR\n([#&#8203;33379](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33379))\n- **nuxt:** Handle non-immediate `useAsyncData` with different key on\nssr ([#&#8203;33341](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33341))\n\n##### 💅 Refactors\n\n- **nuxt:** Improve implementation of error composables\n([#&#8203;33234](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33234))\n- **nuxt:** Resolve path of `typed-router.d.ts` early for consistency\n([#&#8203;33285](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33285))\n- **nuxt:** Place `filename` into `componentsIslandsTemplate` definition\n([#&#8203;33394](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33394))\n- **nuxt,vite:** Use environment-api compatible plugins\n([#&#8203;33403](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33403))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Update usage instructions for Windows users\n([#&#8203;33284](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33284))\n- Remove d suffix in example\n([#&#8203;33298](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33298))\n- Move directory structure to top-level\n([#&#8203;33299](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33299))\n- Add `3.x` prefix to all internal links\n([0fef864d6](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/0fef864d6))\n- Add information about `useFetch` reactivity\n([#&#8203;33317](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33317))\n- Lint code samples within docs\n([#&#8203;33271](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33271))\n- Note `prepare` command `NODE_ENV` behavior\n([#&#8203;33330](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33330))\n- Update `nuxt` command pages\n([#&#8203;33336](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33336))\n\n##### 🏡 Chore\n\n- Update bundle size test\n([15334d0c1](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/15334d0c1))\n- Temporarily disable link to github sponsors\n([53b02251f](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/53b02251f))\n- Update markdownlint ignore\n([557656e54](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/557656e54))\n- Migrate pnpm settings out of `.npmrc`\n([101682a6b](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/101682a6b))\n- Ignore errors from npmjs\n([d56790347](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/d56790347))\n- **nuxt:** Align global components indent\n([#&#8203;33340](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33340))\n- Remove tea.yaml\n([8b2188848](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/8b2188848))\n- Remove todo comment as resolved\n([#&#8203;33389](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33389))\n- Downgrade nitropack in vite\n([3419f3414](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/3419f3414))\n\n##### ✅ Tests\n\n- **nuxt:** Set locale to en for nuxt-time tests\n([#&#8203;33343](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33343))\n- Double `gotoPath` timeout in CI\n([9d336cc76](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/9d336cc76))\n\n##### 🤖 CI\n\n- Add provenance action to check for downgrades in provenance\n([18ab6e5fa](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/18ab6e5fa))\n- Pass commit sha when triggering ecosystem ci\n([7b2949a3c](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/7b2949a3c))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- 山吹色御守 ([@&#8203;KazariEX](https://redirect.github.com/KazariEX))\n- Julien Huang\n([@&#8203;huang-julien](https://redirect.github.com/huang-julien))\n- Florian Heuberger\n([@&#8203;Flo0806](https://redirect.github.com/Flo0806))\n- Ondrej Brendy\n([@&#8203;bandiasek](https://redirect.github.com/bandiasek))\n- Octavio Araiza\n([@&#8203;8ctavio](https://redirect.github.com/8ctavio))\n- Alex Liu\n([@&#8203;Mini-ghost](https://redirect.github.com/Mini-ghost))\n- Bobbie Goede\n([@&#8203;BobbieGoede](https://redirect.github.com/BobbieGoede))\n- abeer0 ([@&#8203;iiio2](https://redirect.github.com/iiio2))\n- Harlan Wilton\n([@&#8203;harlan-zw](https://redirect.github.com/harlan-zw))\n- Alexander Lichter\n([@&#8203;TheAlexLichter](https://redirect.github.com/TheAlexLichter))\n- Sébastien Chopin\n([@&#8203;atinux](https://redirect.github.com/atinux))\n- Ben Hong\n([@&#8203;bencodezen](https://redirect.github.com/bencodezen))\n- Huseyn Guliyev ([@&#8203;husayt](https://redirect.github.com/husayt))\n\n###\n[`v3.19.2`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.19.2)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.19.1...v3.19.2)\n\n> **3.19.2** is a regularly scheduled patch release.\n\n#### ✅ Upgrading\n\nOur recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxt upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis will deduplicate your lockfile as well, and help ensure that you\npull in updates from other dependencies that Nuxt relies on,\nparticularly in the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.19.1...v3.19.2)\n\n##### 🔥 Performance\n\n- **kit:** Do not normalise templates in loop if `dst` is present\n([#&#8203;33200](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33200))\n- **nuxt:** Remove watcher from `hydrate-when` lazy hydration strategy\n([#&#8203;33199](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33199))\n- **nuxt,schema:** Normalise components + directories more efficiently\n([#&#8203;33207](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33207))\n- **kit,nuxt:** Reduce unnecessary iteration in nuxt code\n([#&#8203;33212](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33212))\n- **nuxt:** Skip running lazy hydration transform with filter\n([#&#8203;33213](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33213))\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **schema:** Add `pkg-types` to dependencies\n([a6e5dd756](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/a6e5dd756))\n- **nuxt:** Ignore errors when treeshaking composables within other\ncomposables\n([e3e42ac77](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/e3e42ac77))\n- **nuxt:** Do not tree-shake composables within other composables\n([#&#8203;33153](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33153))\n- **kit:** Ensure module dependencies are typed correctly\n([ea16d182a](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ea16d182a))\n- **nuxt:** Prevent Infinity `backgroundSize` in loading indicator\n([#&#8203;33211](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33211))\n- **nuxt:** Remove unused `enabled` from components dir options\n([#&#8203;32844](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32844))\n- **nuxt:** Sync watch request in useAsyncData\n([#&#8203;33192](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33192))\n- **nuxt:** Move key imports logic after all modules run\n([#&#8203;33214](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33214))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Update language on bridge head migration\n([32e76f609](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/32e76f609))\n\n##### 🏡 Chore\n\n- **nuxt:** Unpin tinyglobby\n([1811db080](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/1811db080))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- Adrien Foulon\n([@&#8203;Tofandel](https://redirect.github.com/Tofandel))\n- Matej Černý\n([@&#8203;cernymatej](https://redirect.github.com/cernymatej))\n- Антон Стасюк\n([@&#8203;11Alone11](https://redirect.github.com/11Alone11))\n- wuiyang ([@&#8203;wuiyang](https://redirect.github.com/wuiyang))\n\n###\n[`v3.19.1`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.19.1)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.19.0...v3.19.1)\n\n> **v3.19.1** is a regularly scheduled patch release\n\n#### ✅ Upgrading\n\nOur recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxt upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis will deduplicate your lockfile as well, and help ensure that you\npull in updates from other dependencies that Nuxt relies on,\nparticularly in the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.19.0...v3.19.1)\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Correct relative path of auto imported components\n([#&#8203;33122](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33122))\n- **nuxt:** Prefer accessing `globalThis` over `window`\n([#&#8203;33125](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33125))\n- **nuxt:** Migrate to AST-aware tree-shaking + route injection\n([#&#8203;33128](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33128))\n- **nuxt:** Ignore #components import mapping inside packages that use\nit internally\n([#&#8203;33049](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33049))\n- **vite:** Remove explicit vite-node configuration of `deps.inline`\n([#&#8203;33133](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33133))\n- **nuxt:** Include trace in dev-time `useRoute` usage warning\n([#&#8203;33039](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33039))\n- **nuxt:** Print route middleware path in warning\n([#&#8203;33136](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33136))\n- **nuxt:** Include core auto-imports from `imports:sources` in override\nwarning\n([#&#8203;33050](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33050))\n- **nuxt:** Render relative importmap entry path if required\n([#&#8203;33146](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33146))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Add documentation for module lifecycle hooks\n([#&#8203;33115](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33115))\n- Add `--` to bun create command\n([ab6aa8ee5](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ab6aa8ee5))\n- Add JSDoc for `navigateTo`\n([#&#8203;21442](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/21442))\n\n##### 🏡 Chore\n\n- Correct `rou3` github url\n([#&#8203;33130](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33130))\n- Include `.ts` extension\n([2c905f864](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/2c905f864))\n\n##### ✅ Tests\n\n- Bump bundle size\n([15564deb9](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/15564deb9))\n- Remove `app/` prefix for tree-shaken composables\n([06ea91705](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/06ea91705))\n\n##### 🤖 CI\n\n- Remove default discord reactions from thread (more noise than it''s\nworth)\n([2e3c91e0c](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/2e3c91e0c))\n- Rewrite release workflow in ts + support multiple tags\n([478c64342](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/478c64342))\n- Pass correct flag\n([a954f383f](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/a954f383f))\n- Pass tag via env variable\n([dcfc82688](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/dcfc82688))\n- Drop `4x` tags from releases\n([e3aa50d11](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/e3aa50d11))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- Matej Černý\n([@&#8203;cernymatej](https://redirect.github.com/cernymatej))\n- Bobbie Goede\n([@&#8203;BobbieGoede](https://redirect.github.com/BobbieGoede))\n- Octavio Araiza\n([@&#8203;8ctavio](https://redirect.github.com/8ctavio))\n- Michael Brevard\n([@&#8203;GalacticHypernova](https://redirect.github.com/GalacticHypernova))\n- abeer0 ([@&#8203;iiio2](https://redirect.github.com/iiio2))\n- 山吹色御守 ([@&#8203;KazariEX](https://redirect.github.com/KazariEX))\n\n###\n[`v3.19.0`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.19.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.18.1...v3.19.0)\n\n#### 👀 Highlights\n\nPlease see the release notes for [Nuxt\nv4.1](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v4.1.0) for\nfull details on the features and fixes in Nuxt v3.19.\n\n#### ✅ Upgrading\n\nAs usual, our recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxt upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis will refresh your lockfile and pull in all the latest dependencies\nthat Nuxt relies on, especially from the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.18.1...v3.19.0)\n\n##### 🚀 Enhancements\n\n- **kit:** Add `ignore` option to `resolveFiles`\n([#&#8203;32858](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32858))\n- **kit:** Add `onInstall` and `onUpgrade` module hooks\n([#&#8203;32397](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32397))\n- **nuxt,vite:** Add experimental support for `rolldown-vite`\n([#&#8203;31812](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/31812))\n- **nuxt:** Extract `defineRouteRules` to page `rules` property\n([#&#8203;32897](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32897))\n- **nuxt,vite:** Use importmap to increase chunk stability\n([#&#8203;33075](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33075))\n- **nuxt:** Lazy hydration macros without auto-imports\n([#&#8203;33037](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33037))\n- **kit,nuxt,schema:** Allow modules to specify dependencies\n([#&#8203;33063](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33063))\n- **kit,nuxt:** Add `getLayerDirectories` util and refactor to use it\n([#&#8203;33098](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33098))\n\n##### 🔥 Performance\n\n- **nuxt:** Clear inline route rules cache when pages change\n([#&#8203;32877](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32877))\n- **nuxt:** Stop watching app manifest once a change has been detected\n([#&#8203;32880](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32880))\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Handle `satisfies` in page augmentation\n([#&#8203;32902](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32902))\n- **nuxt:** Type response in `useFetch` hooks\n([#&#8203;32891](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32891))\n- **nuxt:** Add TS parenthesis and as expression for page meta\nextraction\n([#&#8203;32914](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32914))\n- **nuxt:** Use correct unit thresholds for relative time\n([#&#8203;32893](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32893))\n- **nuxt:** Handle uncached current build manifests\n([#&#8203;32913](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32913))\n- **kit:** Resolve directories in `resolvePath` and normalize file\nextensions\n([#&#8203;32857](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32857))\n- **schema,vite:** Bump `requestTimeout` + allow configuration\n([#&#8203;32874](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32874))\n- **nuxt:** Deep merge extracted route meta\n([#&#8203;32887](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32887))\n- **nuxt:** Do not expose app components until fully resolved\n([#&#8203;32993](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32993))\n- **kit:** Only exclude `node_modules/` if no custom `srcDir`\n([#&#8203;32987](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32987))\n- **nuxt:** Compare final matched routes when syncing `route` object\n([#&#8203;32899](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32899))\n- **nuxt:** Make vue server warnings much less verbose in dev mode\n([#&#8203;33018](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33018))\n- **schema:** Allow disabling cssnano/autoprefixer postcss plugins\n([#&#8203;33016](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33016))\n- **kit:** Ensure local layers are prioritised alphabetically\n([#&#8203;33030](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33030))\n- **kit,nuxt:** Expose global types to vue compiler\n([#&#8203;33026](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33026))\n- **nuxt:** Support config type inference for\n`defineNuxtModule().with()`\n([#&#8203;33081](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33081))\n- **nuxt:** Search for colliding names in route children\n([31a9282c2](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/31a9282c2))\n- **nuxt:** Delete `nuxtApp._runningTransition` on resolve\n([#&#8203;33025](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33025))\n- **nuxt:** Add validation for nuxt island reviver key\n([#&#8203;33069](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33069))\n- **kit:** Prioritise local layers over extended layers\n([ae8b0d2b8](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ae8b0d2b8))\n- **kit:** Address merge conflict\n([89ccbbebb](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/89ccbbebb))\n- **kit:** Do not resolve public dir aliases\n([5d87d3a80](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/5d87d3a80))\n\n##### 💅 Refactors\n\n- **nuxt:** Simplify page segment parsing\n([#&#8203;32901](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32901))\n- **nuxt:** Remove unnecessary `async/await` in `afterEach`\n([#&#8203;32999](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32999))\n- **vite:** Simplify inline chunk iteration\n([9ea90fc33](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/9ea90fc33))\n- **kit,nuxt,ui-templates,vite:** Address deprecations + improve regexp\nperf ([#&#8203;33093](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33093))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Add a section about augmenting types with TS project references\n([#&#8203;32843](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32843))\n- Switch example to use vitest projects\n([#&#8203;32863](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32863))\n- Update testing `setupTimeout` and add `teardownTimeout`\n([#&#8203;32868](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32868))\n- Add middleware to layers guide\n([fa516d440](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/fa516d440))\n- Add documentation for `--nightly` command\n([#&#8203;32907](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32907))\n- Update package information in roadmap section\n([#&#8203;32881](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32881))\n- Add more info about nuxt spa loader element attributes\n([#&#8203;32871](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32871))\n- Correct filename in example\n([#&#8203;33000](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33000))\n- Add more information about using `useRoute` and accessing route in\nmiddleware\n([#&#8203;33004](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33004))\n- Avoid variable shadowing in locale example\n([#&#8203;33031](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33031))\n\n##### 🏡 Chore\n\n- Remove stray test file\n([42fd247a4](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/42fd247a4))\n- Ignore webpagetest.org when scanning links\n([cb18f4960](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/cb18f4960))\n- Add `type: ''module''` in playground\n([#&#8203;33099](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33099))\n\n##### ✅ Tests\n\n- Add failing test for link component duplication\n([#&#8203;32792](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32792))\n- Simplify module hook tests\n([#&#8203;32950](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32950))\n- Refactor stubbing of `import.meta.dev`\n([#&#8203;33023](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33023))\n- Use `findWorkspaceDir` rather than relative paths to repo root\n([c4c3ada96](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/c4c3ada96))\n- Improve router test for global transitions\n([7e6a6fc35](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/7e6a6fc35))\n- Use `expect.poll`\n([f4354203a](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/f4354203a))\n- Use `expect.poll` instead of `expectWithPolling`\n([15ca5be95](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/15ca5be95))\n- Use `vi.waitUntil` instead of custom retry logic\n([4c8c13090](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/4c8c13090))\n- Update test for app creation\n([9a3b44515](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/9a3b44515))\n- Update bundle size snapshot\n([76988ce97](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/76988ce97))\n\n##### 🤖 CI\n\n- Remove double set of tests for docs prs\n([14c006ac4](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/14c006ac4))\n- Add workflow for discord team discussion threads\n([f14854fc3](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/f14854fc3))\n- Fix some syntax issues with discord + github integrations\n([c059f7cd1](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/c059f7cd1))\n- Use token for adding issue to project\n([51661bac3](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/51661bac3))\n- Use discord bot to create thread automatically\n([37f9eb27b](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/37f9eb27b))\n- Only use discord bot\n([38ce2dcbb](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/38ce2dcbb))\n- Update format of discord message\n([0047b3059](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/0047b3059))\n- Try bolding entire line\n([6e9f40eb9](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/6e9f40eb9))\n- Oops\n([8b044cad2](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/8b044cad2))\n- Add delay after adding each reaction\n([37b7e2108](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/37b7e2108))\n- Use last lts node version for testing\n([98719c065](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/98719c065))\n- Try npm trusted publisher\n([ea33502c3](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ea33502c3))\n- Use npm trusted publisher for main releases\n([31a55437f](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/31a55437f))\n- Change wording\n([#&#8203;32979](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32979))\n- Add github ai moderator\n([#&#8203;33077](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/33077))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- abeer0 ([@&#8203;iiio2](https://redirect.github.com/iiio2))\n- Julien Huang\n([@&#8203;huang-julien](https://redirect.github.com/huang-julien))\n- kyumoon ([@&#8203;kyumoon](https://redirect.github.com/kyumoon))\n- Alexander Lichter\n([@&#8203;TheAlexLichter](https://redirect.github.com/TheAlexLichter))\n- Bobbie Goede\n([@&#8203;BobbieGoede](https://redirect.github.com/BobbieGoede))\n- mustafa60x\n([@&#8203;mustafa60x](https://redirect.github.com/mustafa60x))\n- Matej Černý\n([@&#8203;cernymatej](https://redirect.github.com/cernymatej))\n- Alex Liu\n([@&#8203;Mini-ghost](https://redirect.github.com/Mini-ghost))\n- Amitav Chris Mostafa\n([@&#8203;semibroiled](https://redirect.github.com/semibroiled))\n- Romain Hamel ([@&#8203;romhml](https://redirect.github.com/romhml))\n- Jacky Lam\n([@&#8203;jackylamhk](https://redirect.github.com/jackylamhk))\n- Mukund Shah\n([@&#8203;mukundshah](https://redirect.github.com/mukundshah))\n- Luke Nelson ([@&#8203;luc122c](https://redirect.github.com/luc122c))\n- letianpailove\n([@&#8203;letianpailove](https://redirect.github.com/letianpailove))\n- Erwan Jugand\n([@&#8203;erwanjugand](https://redirect.github.com/erwanjugand))\n- Alexander\n([@&#8203;TheColorman](https://redirect.github.com/TheColorman))\n- Ryota Watanabe\n([@&#8203;wattanx](https://redirect.github.com/wattanx))\n- Yizack Rangel ([@&#8203;Yizack](https://redirect.github.com/Yizack))\n\n###\n[`v3.18.1`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.18.1)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.18.0...v3.18.1)\n\n> 3.18.1 is a regularly scheduled patch release.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.18.0...v3.18.1)\n\n##### 🔥 Performance\n\n- **kit:** Get absolute path from `tinyglobby` in `resolveFiles`\n([#&#8203;32846](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32846))\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Do not throw undefined `error` variable\n([#&#8203;32807](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32807))\n- **vite:** Include tsconfig references during `typeCheck`\n([#&#8203;32835](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32835))\n- **nuxt:** Add sourcemap path transformation for client builds\n([#&#8203;32313](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32313))\n- **nuxt:** Add warning for lazy-hydration missing prefix\n([#&#8203;32832](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32832))\n- **nuxt:** Trigger call once navigation even when no suspense\n([#&#8203;32827](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32827))\n- **webpack:** Handle `null` result from webpack call\n([65aa17158](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/65aa17158))\n- **kit,nuxt:** Use `reverseResolveAlias` for better errors\n([#&#8203;32853](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32853))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Update nightly version references\n([#&#8203;32776](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32776))\n- Improve explanation of global middleware\n([#&#8203;32855](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32855))\n\n##### 🏡 Chore\n\n- Update reproduction help text links\n([#&#8203;32803](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32803))\n- Update pnpm ignored build scripts\n([#&#8203;32849](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32849))\n- Improve internal types\n([f271c66c4](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/f271c66c4))\n\n##### ✅ Tests\n\n- Move tests for `defineNuxtComponent` out of e2e test\n([#&#8203;32848](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32848))\n\n##### 🤖 CI\n\n- Move nightly releases into different concurrency group\n([26f9baa6a](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/26f9baa6a))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- RDistinct ([@&#8203;RDistinct](https://redirect.github.com/RDistinct))\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- Oskar Lebuda\n([@&#8203;OskarLebuda](https://redirect.github.com/OskarLebuda))\n- Peter Budai ([@&#8203;peterbud](https://redirect.github.com/peterbud))\n- Matej Černý\n([@&#8203;cernymatej](https://redirect.github.com/cernymatej))\n- Damian Głowala\n([@&#8203;DamianGlowala](https://redirect.github.com/DamianGlowala))\n- Bobbie Goede\n([@&#8203;BobbieGoede](https://redirect.github.com/BobbieGoede))\n- Robin ([@&#8203;OrbisK](https://redirect.github.com/OrbisK))\n- Bobby ([@&#8203;xanzhu](https://redirect.github.com/xanzhu))\n\n###\n[`v3.18.0`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.18.0)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.17.7...v3.18.0)\n\n> 3.18.0 is the next minor release.\n\n#### 👀 Highlights\n\nA huge thank you to everyone who''s been a part of this release, which is\nmostly about backporting features + bugfixes from Nuxt v4.\n\nOver the next six months, we''ll continue backporting compatible v4\nfeatures and bug fixes, so please keep the feedback coming! ❤️\n\n##### 🧪 Lazy Hydration Macros\n\nBuilding on the delayed hydration support from v3.16, we now support\n**lazy hydration macros**\n([#&#8203;31192](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/31192))!\nThese provide a more ergonomic way to control component hydration:\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nconst LazyHydrationMyComponent = defineLazyHydrationComponent(\n  ''visible'',\n  () => import(''./components/MyComponent.vue'')\n)\n</script>\n<template>\n  <div>\n    <!-- \n      Hydration will be triggered when\n      the element(s) is 100px away from entering the viewport.\n    -->\n    <LazyHydrationMyComponent :hydrate-on-visible=\"{ rootMargin: ''100px'' }\" />\n  </div>\n</template>\n```\n\nThese macros make it possible to use Nuxt''s lazy hydration utilities\nalongside explicit component imports.\n\n##### ♿️ Accessibility Improvements\n\nWe''ve enhanced accessibility by including `<NuxtRouteAnnouncer>` in the\nbuilt-in `app.vue`\n([#&#8203;32621](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32621)).\nThis means page changes will be announced to screen readers, making\nnavigation more accessible for users with visual impairments. (This only\napplies if you do not have an `app.vue` in your project. If you do,\nplease keep `<NuxtRouteAnnouncer>` in your `app.vue`!)\n\n##### 🛠️ Enhanced Development Experience\n\n##### Chrome DevTools Workspace Integration\n\nWe''ve added **Chrome DevTools workspace integration**\n([#&#8203;32084](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32084)),\nallowing you to edit your Nuxt source files directly from Chrome\nDevTools. This creates a better debugging experience where changes made\nin DevTools are reflected in your actual source files.\n\n##### Better Component Type Safety\n\nComponent type safety has been improved with:\n\n- **Typed slots for `<ClientOnly>` and `<DevOnly>`**\n([#&#8203;32707](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32707)) -\nbetter IntelliSense and error checking\n- **Exported `<NuxtTime>` prop types**\n([#&#8203;32547](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32547)) -\neasier to extend and customize\n\n##### New Auto-Import: `onWatcherCleanup`\n\nThe `onWatcherCleanup` function from `vue` is now available as an\nauto-import\n([#&#8203;32396](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32396)),\nmaking it easier to clean up watchers and prevent memory leaks:\n\n```ts\nconst { data } = useAsyncData(''users'', fetchUsers)\n\nwatch(data, (newData) => {\n  const interval = setInterval(() => {\n    // Some periodic task\n  }, 1000)\n  \n  // Clean up when the watcher is stopped\n  onWatcherCleanup(() => {\n    clearInterval(interval)\n  })\n})\n```\n\n##### 📊 Observability Enhancements\n\nPage routes are now **exposed to Nitro for observability**\n([#&#8203;32617](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32617)),\nenabling better monitoring and analytics integration with supported\nplatforms. This allows observability tools to track page-level metrics\nmore effectively.\n\n##### 🔧 Module Development Improvements\n\nModule authors get several quality-of-life improvements:\n\n##### Simplified Server Imports\n\nThe `addServerImports` kit utility now **supports single imports**\n([#&#8203;32289](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32289)),\nmaking it easier to add individual server utilities:\n\n```ts\n// Before: had to wrap in array\naddServerImports([{ from: ''my-package'', name: ''myUtility'' }])\n\n// Now: can pass directly\naddServerImports({ from: ''my-package'', name: ''myUtility'' })\n```\n\n##### TypeScript Configuration\n\nModules can now **add to `typescript.hoist`**\n([#&#8203;32601](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32601)),\ngiving them more control over TypeScript configuration and type\ngeneration.\n\n##### ⚡️ Performance Improvements\n\nWe''ve made several performance optimizations:\n\n- **Improved Vite-node communication** via internal socket\n([#&#8203;32417](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32417)) for\nfaster development builds\n- **Migration to `oxc-walker`**\n([#&#8203;32250](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32250)) and\n**oxc for `onPrehydrate` transforms**\n([#&#8203;32045](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32045)) for\nfaster code transformations\n\n##### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n\nThis release also includes several important fixes:\n\n- **Improved data fetching**: When computed keys change, old data is now\nproperly retained\n([#&#8203;32616](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32616))\n- **Better scroll behavior**: `scrollBehaviorType` is now only used for\nhash scrolling\n([#&#8203;32622](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32622))\n- **Fixed directory aliases**: Added trailing slashes to some directory\naliases for better consistency\n([#&#8203;32755](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32755))\n\n##### ✅ Upgrading\n\nAs usual, our recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxi@latest upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis refreshes your lockfile and pulls in all the latest dependencies\nthat Nuxt relies on, especially from the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.17.7...v3.18.0)\n\n##### 🚀 Enhancements\n\n- **nuxt:** Expose page routes to nitro for o11y\n([#&#8203;32617](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32617))\n- **nuxt:** Export `<NuxtTime>` prop types\n([#&#8203;32547](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32547))\n- **nuxt:** Add integration with chrome devtools workspaces\n([#&#8203;32084](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32084))\n- **kit:** Support single import in `addServerImports`\n([#&#8203;32289](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32289))\n- **nuxt:** Add `onWatcherCleanup` to imports presets\n([#&#8203;32396](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32396))\n- **nuxt:** Add route announcer to default app.vue\n([#&#8203;32621](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32621))\n- **nuxt:** Support lazy hydration macros\n([#&#8203;31192](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/31192))\n\n##### 🔥 Performance\n\n- **vite:** Communicate with vite-node via internal socket\n([#&#8203;32417](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32417))\n- **kit:** Update env expansion regex to match nitro\n([#&#8203;30766](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/30766))\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Allow modules to add to `typescript.hoist`\n([#&#8203;32601](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32601))\n- **nuxt:** Retain old data when computed key changes\n([#&#8203;32616](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32616))\n- **nuxt:** Only use `scrollBehaviorType` for hash scrolling\n([#&#8203;32622](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32622))\n- **nuxt:** Add missing `async`\n([fd312af03](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/fd312af03))\n- **nuxt:** Fix transform/minify types + bump oxc-transform\n([d2ba19963](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/d2ba19963))\n- **nuxt:** Provide typed slots for `<ClientOnly>` and `<DevOnly>`\n([#&#8203;32707](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32707))\n- **kit,nuxt,schema:** Add trailing slash to some dir aliases\n([#&#8203;32755](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32755))\n- **nuxt:** Include source base url for remote islands\n([#&#8203;32772](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32772))\n- **vite:** Use vite node server to transform requests\n([#&#8203;32791](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32791))\n- **kit:** Use `mlly` to parse module paths\n([#&#8203;32386](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32386))\n- **nuxt:** Execute all plugins after error rendering error.vue\n([#&#8203;32744](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32744))\n\n##### 💅 Refactors\n\n- **nuxt:** Migrate to `oxc-walker`\n([#&#8203;32250](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32250))\n- **nuxt,schema:** Use oxc for `onPrehydrate` transform\n([#&#8203;32045](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32045))\n- **nuxt:** Pass file language directly to parser options\n([#&#8203;32665](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32665))\n- **nuxt:** Use direct import of `installNuxtModule`\n([228e3585e](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/228e3585e))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Pass `v3` template to create nuxt examples\n([03182202f](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/03182202f))\n- Add reference to `useNuxtData` in data fetching composable pages\n([#&#8203;32589](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32589))\n- Document the --modules flag in the init command\n([#&#8203;32599](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32599))\n- Added new Shared folder to the example of v4 folder structure\n([#&#8203;32630](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32630))\n- Improve grammar\n([#&#8203;32640](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32640))\n- Typos\n([#&#8203;32567](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32567))\n- Fix abbreviation\n([#&#8203;32613](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32613))\n- Reference `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` rule change in v4 guide\n([#&#8203;32643](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32643))\n- Fix links to Nitro docs\n([#&#8203;32691](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32691))\n- Add best practices section\n([#&#8203;31609](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/31609))\n- Correct alias for local fonts in styling guide\n([#&#8203;32680](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32680))\n- Update nuxt.new links to v4\n([#&#8203;32639](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32639))\n- Set correct default value for deep option in usefetch\n([#&#8203;32724](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32724))\n- Fix link to issue\n([ca03f533f](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ca03f533f))\n- Add AI-assisted contribution guidelines\n([#&#8203;32725](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32725))\n- Update Nuxt installation command to use `npm create nuxt@latest`\n([#&#8203;32726](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32726))\n- Hydration best practice\n([#&#8203;32746](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32746))\n- Add example for module `.with()`\n([#&#8203;32757](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32757))\n- Replace dead Vue Router docs links\n([#&#8203;32779](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32779))\n\n##### 🏡 Chore\n\n- Handle missing commit details\n([0af98763d](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/0af98763d))\n- Update reproduction links for bug-report template\n([#&#8203;32722](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32722))\n- Update `unbuild` and use absolute path in dev stubs\n([#&#8203;32759](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32759))\n\n##### ✅ Tests\n\n- Also assert status\n([4b4b224f7](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/4b4b224f7))\n- Ignore vue `module.exports` export\n([ac8b02d09](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ac8b02d09))\n- Extend timeout when waiting for hydration\n([49c01ba81](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/49c01ba81))\n- Benchmark minimal fixture instead\n([#&#8203;31174](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/31174))\n- Add minimal pages fixture\n([#&#8203;30457](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/30457))\n- Bump bundle size\n([bafa953c3](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/bafa953c3))\n\n##### 🤖 CI\n\n- Trigger website redeploy on main branch\n([#&#8203;32695](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32695))\n- Release `pkg.pr.new` for `main`/`3.x` branches as well\n([ca4f0b1da](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/ca4f0b1da))\n- Apply `3x` tag to latest v3 release\n([5e8dfc150](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/5e8dfc150))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- Bobbie Goede\n([@&#8203;BobbieGoede](https://redirect.github.com/BobbieGoede))\n- Damian Głowala\n([@&#8203;DamianGlowala](https://redirect.github.com/DamianGlowala))\n- Dog ([@&#8203;dgxo](https://redirect.github.com/dgxo))\n- Julien Huang\n([@&#8203;huang-julien](https://redirect.github.com/huang-julien))\n- Yauheni Vasiukevich\n([@&#8203;EvgenyWas](https://redirect.github.com/EvgenyWas))\n- Alex Liu\n([@&#8203;Mini-ghost](https://redirect.github.com/Mini-ghost))\n- Robin ([@&#8203;OrbisK](https://redirect.github.com/OrbisK))\n- Mateleo ([@&#8203;Mateleo](https://redirect.github.com/Mateleo))\n- Stephen Jason Wang\n([@&#8203;stephenjason89](https://redirect.github.com/stephenjason89))\n- Maurits Meester\n([@&#8203;mmeester](https://redirect.github.com/mmeester))\n- Igor Kononenko\n([@&#8203;igorexa34314](https://redirect.github.com/igorexa34314))\n- Alex ([@&#8203;hywax](https://redirect.github.com/hywax))\n- Matej Černý\n([@&#8203;cernymatej](https://redirect.github.com/cernymatej))\n- Alexander Lichter\n([@&#8203;TheAlexLichter](https://redirect.github.com/TheAlexLichter))\n- Hashim Kalam\n([@&#8203;hashimkalam](https://redirect.github.com/hashimkalam))\n- Alois Sečkár\n([@&#8203;AloisSeckar](https://redirect.github.com/AloisSeckar))\n- Haythem Frikha\n([@&#8203;Flamenate](https://redirect.github.com/Flamenate))\n- abeer0 ([@&#8203;iiio2](https://redirect.github.com/iiio2))\n- Thomas ([@&#8203;ThomasWT](https://redirect.github.com/ThomasWT))\n- Connor Pearson\n([@&#8203;cjpearson](https://redirect.github.com/cjpearson))\n- dwood-csi ([@&#8203;dwood-csi](https://redirect.github.com/dwood-csi))\n\n###\n[`v3.17.7`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.17.7)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.17.6...v3.17.7)\n\n> 3.17.7 is the last patch release before v3.18.\n\n#### ✅ Upgrading\n\nOur recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxt upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis will deduplicate your lockfile as well, and help ensure that you\npull in updates from other dependencies that Nuxt relies on,\nparticularly in the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.17.6...v3.17.7)\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Safe-guard `extraPageMetaExtractionKeys`\n([#&#8203;32510](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32510))\n- **nuxt:** Expose `loadBuilder` error cause\n([8f13ce3c2](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/8f13ce3c2))\n- **vite:** Handle resolving string vite input\n([#&#8203;32527](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32527))\n- **nuxt:** Wrap only server components with island generic\n([#&#8203;32540](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32540))\n- **vite:** Ignore when client entry cannot be resolved\n([19a292f34](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/19a292f34))\n- **nuxt:** Normalize segment catchall pattern before checking for\nparent\n([#&#8203;32413](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32413))\n- **nuxt:** Update warning message to warn against `null` values\n([c1b83eab5](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/c1b83eab5))\n- **nuxt:** Ensure `semver.satisfies` returns true for pre-release\nversions\n([#&#8203;32574](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32574))\n- **nuxt:** Scroll to anchor if present when changing page without saved\nposition\n([#&#8203;32376](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32376))\n- **nuxt:** Handle `execute being passed to `watch\\`\n([#&#8203;32591](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32591))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Update fetch types\n([#&#8203;32522](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32522))\n- Clarify that runtime env variables must start with `NUXT_`\n([#&#8203;32223](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32223))\n- Fix key change behavior in `useAsyncData` and `useFetch` migration\n([#&#8203;32560](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32560))\n- Change return type of async data from `undefined` to `null` in v3 docs\n([#&#8203;32562](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32562))\n- Add section on custom hooks for Nuxt modules\n([#&#8203;32586](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32586))\n- Provide `async` keyword\n([#&#8203;32587](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32587))\n- Move augmenting hook types in hooks page\n([#&#8203;32595](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32595))\n- Add section about module loading order\n([#&#8203;32597](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32597))\n\n##### ✅ Tests\n\n- Reenable skipped unit tests\n([8fc9b9ee9](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/8fc9b9ee9))\n- Update test snapshot for `generateTypes`\n([c0855439d](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/c0855439d))\n- Improve page scanning test stability\n([84b96f3de](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/84b96f3de))\n- Pass timeZone in to `<NuxtTime>` test\n([#&#8203;32558](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32558))\n- Add more useAsyncData + useFetch tests\n([#&#8203;32585](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32585))\n- Avoid hard-coding async-data keys\n([bfca95118](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/commit/bfca95118))\n\n##### ❤️ Contributors\n\n- Daniel Roe\n([@&#8203;danielroe](https://redirect.github.com/danielroe))\n- Julien Huang\n([@&#8203;huang-julien](https://redirect.github.com/huang-julien))\n- abeer0 ([@&#8203;iiio2](https://redirect.github.com/iiio2))\n- Bobbie Goede\n([@&#8203;BobbieGoede](https://redirect.github.com/BobbieGoede))\n- Damian Głowala\n([@&#8203;DamianGlowala](https://redirect.github.com/DamianGlowala))\n- Nestor Vera ([@&#8203;hacknug](https://redirect.github.com/hacknug))\n- Ezra Ashenafi ([@&#8203;Eazash](https://redirect.github.com/Eazash))\n- Mike Laumann Bellika\n([@&#8203;MikeBellika](https://redirect.github.com/MikeBellika))\n- Maxime Pauvert\n([@&#8203;maximepvrt](https://redirect.github.com/maximepvrt))\n- Chriest Yu ([@&#8203;jcppman](https://redirect.github.com/jcppman))\n- Andrei Hudalla\n([@&#8203;paranoidPhantom](https://redirect.github.com/paranoidPhantom))\n- Sigrid Huemer ([@&#8203;s1gr1d](https://redirect.github.com/s1gr1d))\n- xjccc ([@&#8203;xjccc](https://redirect.github.com/xjccc))\n\n###\n[`v3.17.6`](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/releases/tag/v3.17.6)\n\n[Compare\nSource](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.17.5...v3.17.6)\n\n> 3.17.6 is a regularly scheduled patch release.\n\n#### ✅ Upgrading\n\nOur recommendation for upgrading is to run:\n\n```sh\nnpx nuxt upgrade --dedupe\n```\n\nThis will deduplicate your lockfile as well, and help ensure that you\npull in updates from other dependencies that Nuxt relies on,\nparticularly in the unjs ecosystem.\n\n#### 👉 Changelog\n\n[compare\nchanges](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/compare/v3.17.5...v3.17.6)\n\n##### 🔥 Performance\n\n- **nuxt:** Decrease if checks when prerendering\n([#&#8203;32455](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32455))\n\n##### 🩹 Fixes\n\n- **nuxt:** Generate correct types for async data defaults based on\n`nuxt.config`\n([#&#8203;32324](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32324))\n- **nuxt:** Reload at base URL in `nuxt:chunk-reload-immediate`\n([#&#8203;32382](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32382))\n- **nuxt:** Use rollup to calculate island component filenames\n([#&#8203;32421](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32421))\n- **nuxt:** Append `set-cookie` headers in error handler\n([#&#8203;32483](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32483))\n- **nuxt:** Ensure `asyncData` runs if changing key while fetcher is\nrunning\n([#&#8203;32466](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32466))\n- **nuxt:** Handle pure hash link clicks with `navigateTo`\n([#&#8203;32393](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32393))\n- **nuxt:** Skip external `<NuxtLink>`''s custom on click handler\n([#&#8203;32499](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32499))\n- **nuxt:** Update component loader regexp for minified code\n([#&#8203;32298](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32298))\n- **nuxt:** Allow camelCase for lazy hydration attributes\n([#&#8203;32297](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32297))\n- **nuxt:** Respect `inheritAttrs: false` in `createClientOnly` fn\n([#&#8203;32323](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32323))\n- **kit:** Do not double-urlify file urls when resolving schema\n([#&#8203;32354](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32354))\n- **nuxt:** Align scroll behavior with page transition completion\n([#&#8203;32239](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32239))\n- **nuxt:** Set `output.generatedCode.symbols` for nitro build\n([#&#8203;32358](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32358))\n- **nuxt:** Lazily access runtimeConfig\n([#&#8203;32428](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32428))\n\n##### 💅 Refactors\n\n- **vite:** Migrate plugins internally to vite environments\n([#&#8203;32461](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32461))\n\n##### 📖 Documentation\n\n- Clarify where logging tag is displayed\n([#&#8203;32440](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32440))\n- Remove kit playground auto-import note\n([#&#8203;32415](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32415))\n- Remove webstorm warning\n([#&#8203;32513](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32513))\n- Migrate to `h3js`\n([#&#8203;32243](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32243))\n- Update the fetch `clear` function description\n([#&#8203;32287](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32287))\n- `defineNuxtPlugin` function documentation\n([#&#8203;32328](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32328))\n- Mention that `<NuxtLink>` encodes query params\n([#&#8203;32361](https://redirect.github.com/nuxt/nuxt/pull/32361))\n- Enhance documentation for Nuxt composables\n([#&#8203;32218](https://redirect.github.com/