:"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commits/f16e56d46cd2f0be72baa4d3863328c1f67b1155/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:52:27Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T19:52:27Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Keep the subscription form and report the error when saving fails (#417)\n\n* (fix) Keep the subscription form and report the error when saving fails\n\nSaving the OCL subscription wrote the new values into the SWR cache\noptimistically, then checked `response.ok`. `openmrsFetch` rejects on any\nnon-2xx response, so the error branch was unreachable, and the optimistic\nwrite stored a bare subscription where `useSubscription` expects\n`{ data: { results: [...] } }`. On a failed save the hook read\n`undefined`, the effect cleared every input, no revalidation ran, and the\nonly feedback was the framework''s generic unhandled-error toast.\n\nDrop the optimistic write and wrap the save in try/catch. On failure,\nshow the app''s own error notification with the server message and leave\nthe inputs as typed. On success, revalidate and show the existing success\nmessage.\n\nAlso judge an import upload by its `.zip` extension rather than its MIME\ntype. Browsers report ZIPs as any of the four types the backend accepts,\nor with no type at all, so the old check rejected valid archives on some\nplatforms, while accepting `application/octet-stream` alone would have\nlet any unknown binary through with a message saying only .zip files are\nallowed.\n\n* Show the backend''s reason when saving the subscription fails\n\nThe error notification repeated `openmrsFetch`''s generic \"Server\nresponded with 500\" message. The backend puts its reason in the response\nbody, so show that when it is there and fall back to the fetch error\notherwise.\n\n* Accept uploads by extension only and guard an empty drop\n\nCarbon''s drop container already matches `.zip` by extension and never\ndiscards a file for a MIME mismatch, so the MIME list only widened the\nnative file picker to almost any file. Keep `.zip` as the sole accept\nvalue.\n\nCarbon does discard a file whose name fails its extension pattern, and\nit passes nothing for a drop of non-file content, so `onAddFiles` can\nreceive an empty list. Treat that like any other non-zip drop instead of\nthrowing.\n\nuser-event applies the input''s accept attribute by default, so the test\nturns that off to exercise the component''s own check.\n\n* Narrow the save error to OpenmrsFetchError and translate the fallback\n\nOnly an `OpenmrsFetchError` carries a response body, and only a JSON\nbody carries the backend''s reason. For anything else the old fallback\nshowed the fetch error''s own message, which tells the user to check\n`err.responseBody` or the network tab. Show a translated generic message\ninstead, matching the metadata export delete modal.\n\nThe failing-save test now rejects with a real `OpenmrsFetchError`.","tree":{"sha":"bff7b645d6a50f10269dea3a27c0bafdacd1d30a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/git/trees/bff7b645d6a50f10269dea3a27c0bafdacd1d30a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/git/commits/f16e56d46cd2f0be72baa4d3863328c1f67b1155","verification":{"payload":"tree bff7b645d6a50f10269dea3a27c0bafdacd1d30a\nparent 827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1791402747 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791402747 +0300\n\n(fix) Keep the subscription form and report the error when saving fails (#417)\n\n* (fix) Keep the subscription form and report the error when saving fails\n\nSaving the OCL subscription wrote the new values into the SWR cache\noptimistically, then checked `response.ok`. `openmrsFetch` rejects on any\nnon-2xx response, so the error branch was unreachable, and the optimistic\nwrite stored a bare subscription where `useSubscription` expects\n`{ data: { results: [...] } }`. On a failed save the hook read\n`undefined`, the effect cleared every input, no revalidation ran, and the\nonly feedback was the framework''s generic unhandled-error toast.\n\nDrop the optimistic write and wrap the save in try/catch. On failure,\nshow the app''s own error notification with the server message and leave\nthe inputs as typed. On success, revalidate and show the existing success\nmessage.\n\nAlso judge an import upload by its `.zip` extension rather than its MIME\ntype. Browsers report ZIPs as any of the four types the backend accepts,\nor with no type at all, so the old check rejected valid archives on some\nplatforms, while accepting `application/octet-stream` alone would have\nlet any unknown binary through with a message saying only .zip files are\nallowed.\n\n* Show the backend''s reason when saving the subscription fails\n\nThe error notification repeated `openmrsFetch`''s generic \"Server\nresponded with 500\" message. The backend puts its reason in the response\nbody, so show that when it is there and fall back to the fetch error\notherwise.\n\n* Accept uploads by extension only and guard an empty drop\n\nCarbon''s drop container already matches `.zip` by extension and never\ndiscards a file for a MIME mismatch, so the MIME list only widened the\nnative file picker to almost any file. Keep `.zip` as the sole accept\nvalue.\n\nCarbon does discard a file whose name fails its extension pattern, and\nit passes nothing for a drop of non-file content, so `onAddFiles` can\nreceive an empty list. Treat that like any other non-zip drop instead of\nthrowing.\n\nuser-event applies the input''s accept attribute by default, so the test\nturns that off to exercise the component''s own check.\n\n* Narrow the save error to OpenmrsFetchError and translate the fallback\n\nOnly an `OpenmrsFetchError` carries a response body, and only a JSON\nbody carries the backend''s reason. For anything else the old fallback\nshowed the fetch error''s own message, which tells the user to check\n`err.responseBody` or the network tab. Show a translated generic message\ninstead, matching the metadata export delete modal.\n\nThe failing-save test now rejects with a real `OpenmrsFetchError`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxqL7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAGOMQALHiGW1su0MRkcHjXiaz84EW\nxyWb0/o2DiiHcGwZkuWkl7tT8nY+xf/9PZOzbOKAHMYvgaud+20UKqHPfCsUI0dP\nRfGG/HvamcxO2rwDAzdSWAiYouu7hPaeBeABCQN7EQcxlECj5moLSKRfVhuS3eFq\nvr911jiN83NtjuLYpebszu1fqFrAta9ujL+8DWT7zx3gN4IFH/T0374oG4Zh7oNV\nDATRF80EoLBz4RcgGrDQvnsRoBD56zeP1n5/PN0jR0NehxSTLdQ3K0lmUIEgPxuj\nBsRJvcyaqVzOiHYI2ooH8Ihkhdx+Ky4C1zqjw6aDlw19p4ML1fh7JmsXMQDb9LPc\nvlreeY1blwcsJayfJCuvmx0RdZNdRoyo4dyCdjw+bJWBizEGv7Bnq5/ijqo0BgN9\nG02ZixjG7CxOvBbf+UnL1aUwHh9kilGV0j1/eq4YyjzADyFyzrJMUkAmUim88ai5\nYjVl70H3f5+7V84q1aUz/4vScnHiutfwXmFAfHCVDs6RdzuSBxMl8oe1gUY/Ft01\nPkHrqR/e7Tr9ePIDddJrVDRh80iQJymGVjOFrZEPnrl8Gwhkz6u9XJ2Y7JnsRfrU\nZ+bvN33YUKDo2Uo+ANCUA3kiohCg+9IONJBv5jGB7GHsRPQ0fFAQ+60GVgbrX5U+\nfRPlr51/wvv1pZc6ZGd4\n=qxL1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-07T19:52:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commit/f16e56d46cd2f0be72baa4d3863328c1f67b1155","node_id":"C_kwDOGtwHTdoAKGYxNmU1NmQ0NmNkMmYwYmU3MmJhYTRkMzg2MzMyOGMxZjY3YjExNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commit/827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","sha":"827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commits/827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9"}],"sha":"f16e56d46cd2f0be72baa4d3863328c1f67b1155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commits/f16e56d46cd2f0be72baa4d3863328c1f67b1155"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8509731?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/denniskigen","id":8509731,"login":"denniskigen","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1MDk3MzE=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/denniskigen","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/commits/827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:48:50Z","email":"kigen.work@gmail.com","name":"Dennis Kigen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T18:48:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)\n\n* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\n\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\n\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\n\n* Keep the cron editor''s floated fields inside its wrapper\n\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor''s wrapper only had a height\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\nwrapper contain them in any parent.","tree":{"sha":"aff54efa553656b731aca3eafbd5d5dbac16b564","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/git/trees/aff54efa553656b731aca3eafbd5d5dbac16b564"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openmrs/openmrs-esm-admin-tools/git/commits/827b70e647d060eaf53b478c1bebd8987b7a00d9","verification":{"payload":"tree aff54efa553656b731aca3eafbd5d5dbac16b564\nparent 62fb97e7ddb68b412c276d1e49914c5c119b6015\nauthor Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com> 1791398930 +0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791398930 +0000\n\n(fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack (#423)\n\n* (fix) Space the report form fields evenly with a Carbon Stack\n\nThe run report and edit scheduled report forms now put their fields in\na Stack with gap={5}, and the form container sets the 16px padding.\nBefore, each field set its own spacing: fixed heights with\n30px bottom margins, an extra 50px margin and 32px top padding on the\noutput format select, and 16px padding on each parameter and the cron\neditor. That left uneven gaps between the fields.\n\nThe Report and Output format selects also lose their fixed 300px width,\nso every field in both forms is full width like the parameter inputs.\n\n* Keep the cron editor''s floated fields inside its wrapper\n\nThe schedule fields float, so the editor''s wrapper only had a height\nbecause the Stack around it is a grid. display: flow-root makes the\nwrapper contain them in any parent.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxpQSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9vIQAA9hs1ne1+hhyz6R4bBLxmBL\n95D+kejiTroVW4p/O6wxE/bm//S/tB+FhjtHatVItn4lF7IdRf2uDRBe8QEXBUob\ns+B6PUlzO9KPa+YRZbzcL8kmGzv15uEMoDyc94sebeeZPUZzVCi9I7pLyb9dRJbx\nFNeKmgWiOc62DdBPNmGZJT5OK/MtICaT8NMAIujGLBX3iJSFc8/5RFM1EKrO6ESm\nDsblBzxI1vglV9E2Ql5oGmdfeH5gms4eA1VtX07we3tDLz15sUS7n+G4+/ERfoZV\nC9tZfF/cpDeiy4dHswF53XZeqa215HQpccdXY92V71tgcki6aheKNkfPnLhNWcdj\nk5Eo+Xeu7+wJlPrCPgY6/uyfFk9JuPCcjVqRQcLp8K+8l0dibBVpQy/MShiowxti\nIFBTcjXJodKng