":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a52617b21a61354d6e9149211dcaa3788fd7a935/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:59:23Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:59:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Reformat with Prettier 3 (#1177)\n\nFormatting only (`npm run format`). Prettier 3 changed rules that have\nno option to keep the old style: nested ternary indentation, parens\naround `??` in ternaries, short unions on one line, multi-value SCSS\n`transition:` split over lines. Doing it in one commit keeps these\nchanges out of unrelated diffs via the pre-commit hook.\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e192625d5e654d5ffa882e0fc776270d607a6d75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/e192625d5e654d5ffa882e0fc776270d607a6d75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/a52617b21a61354d6e9149211dcaa3788fd7a935","verification":{"payload":"tree e192625d5e654d5ffa882e0fc776270d607a6d75\nparent a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790949563 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790949563 +0200\n\nReformat with Prettier 3 (#1177)\n\nFormatting only (`npm run format`). Prettier 3 changed rules that have\nno option to keep the old style: nested ternary indentation, parens\naround `??` in ternaries, short unions on one line, multi-value SCSS\n`transition:` split over lines. Doing it in one commit keeps these\nchanges out of unrelated diffs via the pre-commit hook.\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv7i7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuDgQAEsTs4DS+hw09XZIPjE4zmHT\nbBoSeOvIJy9wPK3JTAg+ELEYSxptwcGoGSRzyk7vmVz9BVb79N6RmgeQnuBlj5uQ\nojX1q3mK6Bbc2E1rCbGeXMHLr7PHI+MumLMZbvtKKM0Cn/5Qn6zxszAfYijQkOe6\nOS5MWA1JsJkgG8JVlCkla1bh2mVbxAEnt7QyMo/R+eTU1zisbjKiSm+kp7r7QiaS\nx8mV4lBp2cBilhAH7PmGO7kmXCam8CXc4MMiDX0LZHxoGcKSKGBmCDQXqzUO617F\nwOR5agVYesxOAvIXP4MCTym4SEjaQJliKK/T1U8FON52Zdwfc528AODzzch/eJ9J\nUvv/WO74Bt92qqDPqL1kJRGErvnTt+QJAKlKhv/OIhhFcCJbSxTrlpwoxlIps8YO\nOJrfKKuX/LOQf2FOJgl5ktjrR8fRMEdU01t5/OwTXjCo69tR4lk0xcPHMcKqX0UV\nXqyml3bxNRzzlplqLDK0SzQGvadnlTBp0CGgiPLCXKWm3wsPcOxu59xRNXYI7biJ\n+RGJ1NTK34oudibGjF326P51SJ7wYKd/E//3a5pNuEnTJ+NhXSNfTCMOgDOfWUiB\npqK3R3A7/S9qTuW3PrPyUGK+oYoAUF8URCrubr9ircUW2cdsod3RwX5HIBzoUfU0\n+lj77t0BMQBH8QZr4Tr8\n=QN0D\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:59:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/a52617b21a61354d6e9149211dcaa3788fd7a935","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGE1MjYxN2IyMWE2MTM1NGQ2ZTkxNDkyMTFkY2FhMzc4OGZkN2E5MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d","sha":"a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d"}],"sha":"a52617b21a61354d6e9149211dcaa3788fd7a935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a52617b21a61354d6e9149211dcaa3788fd7a935"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:16:04Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:16:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enable the React Compiler (#1171)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Enable the React Compiler\n\nTurn on Next''s built-in React Compiler support (reactCompiler: true,\nbacked by babel-plugin-react-compiler 1.0) so components get automatic\nmemoization instead of relying on hand-written useMemo/useCallback.\n\nThe compiler is conservative: any component or hook that breaks the\nRules of React in a way it can detect (ref reads during render, mutating\nprops/hook values, unsupported syntax, react-hook-form''s watch(), etc.)\nis skipped and runs exactly as before. Those are the same spots already\nflagged by the react-hooks/* compiler lint rules that eslint-config-next\nships, so the lint output is unchanged. Of ~280 components/hooks, ~230\ncompile and ~50 are skipped.\n\nThe donation widget''s redux reducers are fully immutable, so memoizing on\nselector results is safe; a headless run of the widget pane flows\n(single bank, recurring Vipps, custom share, validation/back) produced\nidentical results and request payloads before and after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Opt usePaneTransition out of the React Compiler\n\nThe compiler memoized the `paneRefs` array literal in usePaneTransition\ntogether with the four useRef calls inside it, so after the first render\nthose hooks were skipped. React then saw a different hook order and threw\n\"Should have a queue\" (minified #311), crashing every /innsamling/*\nfundraiser page with \"Application error\" (29 pages on the NO site; caught\nby the fundraiser-widget Cypress spec).\n\n\"use no memo\" keeps the hook exactly as it behaved before the compiler.\nRestructuring the refs instead would make `paneRefs` referentially stable\nand change how often useMultipleElementHeights re-measures, which is a\nbehaviour change better made deliberately. A scan of the compiled output\nof every component/hook found no other hook calls inside memo blocks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6ff88175a4a66d7d21e89fee6dda1c87fe18bbb4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/6ff88175a4a66d7d21e89fee6dda1c87fe18bbb4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d","verification":{"payload":"tree 6ff88175a4a66d7d21e89fee6dda1c87fe18bbb4\nparent a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790946964 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790946964 +0200\n\nEnable the React Compiler (#1171)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Enable the React Compiler\n\nTurn on Next''s built-in React Compiler support (reactCompiler: true,\nbacked by babel-plugin-react-compiler 1.0) so components get automatic\nmemoization instead of relying on hand-written useMemo/useCallback.\n\nThe compiler is conservative: any component or hook that breaks the\nRules of React in a way it can detect (ref reads during render, mutating\nprops/hook values, unsupported syntax, react-hook-form''s watch(), etc.)\nis skipped and runs exactly as before. Those are the same spots already\nflagged by the react-hooks/* compiler lint rules that eslint-config-next\nships, so the lint output is unchanged. Of ~280 components/hooks, ~230\ncompile and ~50 are skipped.\n\nThe donation widget''s redux reducers are fully immutable, so memoizing on\nselector results is safe; a headless run of the widget pane flows\n(single bank, recurring Vipps, custom share, validation/back) produced\nidentical results and request payloads before and after.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Opt usePaneTransition out of the React Compiler\n\nThe compiler memoized the `paneRefs` array literal in usePaneTransition\ntogether with the four useRef calls inside it, so after the first render\nthose hooks were skipped. React then saw a different hook order and threw\n\"Should have a queue\" (minified #311), crashing every /innsamling/*\nfundraiser page with \"Application error\" (29 pages on the NO site; caught\nby the fundraiser-widget Cypress spec).\n\n\"use no memo\" keeps the hook exactly as it behaved before the compiler.\nRestructuring the refs instead would make `paneRefs` referentially stable\nand change how often useMultipleElementHeights re-measures, which is a\nbehaviour change better made deliberately. A scan of the compiled output\nof every component/hook found no other hook calls inside memo blocks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv66UCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4Y8QAAYLk5Dnn/c+DxbCvpmqsqGA\na4tKmIkOpq1msEp+CeVFFogoVUQBGRPnXeWsyCdzagn0Cw7aLIf5suPg2S+n4AMK\nCWQwyJTTx5z1ztSl1k9+pSIJqB7cm0rjsVFg/aWwTrhE3/tSRbksfzgtlA+NVOMk\nE3kY/SMrGwJWpM78CIbuR3chI4d2hnPCbgZWs4zXBsxhr8q51IX4DHX60VnEjgiR\nNY8D5OeG5dFPsDmwqhFtBBO5HAIJseojbcfFxGTjiBpz+rblQtvEeAqxIcXab2nZ\nnV1zTPwGinwJ22SOL7zgrIQSc3BdfIJFt2pyDxW9RvNaBJsXJYT2aikJBrxUVHRo\nRH67zquuAHRMEI7v9hWQUKKfIU/wxjDx5ayBDGs1a0RwuSNohUMbwMra3sSHfgG+\n33VlyjQGmV+jMJ6jJeLBZcA544DfKvQ61i86ruB8bEQE1iAN7FH37+r26OYoq3ge\n4+vbWeXqcZHBRnC5DEz8iE/U5imrt8n29lbiZMKxW1gA7ogqjm6s+kuknGdQYJG/\nckak64ijAWnvoX9hDyrJTcH15udjpJcZYVaGZ5mnL2jbJcuFnBc8FH3hgAm5UPfu\ntZUYXRu6rhWRxNjGzUWDqoGAk15CZx0DS6PlbsZG2NBxNKM7aOFmLwIGSRmhkjPp\nnXWeZaK5/aCWk1itOs6d\n=iJPN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:16:04Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGE5MmI1MjM5ZDRkNDQzODIzNzEwNWIyMDdkYjQ5MDlhOWQzYjY5MGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07","sha":"a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07"}],"sha":"a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a92b5239d4d4438237105b207db4909a9d3b690d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:08:52Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:08:52Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade Sanity Studio to v6 and React 19 (#1173)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Sanity Studio to v6 and React 19\n\nBump the Studio in studio/ to the current majors:\n- sanity and @sanity/vision 4.22 -> 6.17\n- react / react-dom 18.3 -> 19.3 (Studio v5+ requires React >= 19.2)\n- @sanity/ui 3.5 -> 4.3, @sanity/table 1.1 -> 3.1\n- add @sanity/icons ^5.2 as an explicit dependency, since our custom\n  inputs import from it directly\n\nBreaking changes handled:\n- @sanity/ui v4 removed the deprecated `space` prop (now `gap`) and the\n  Grid `columns` / `rows` props (now `gridTemplateColumns` /\n  `gridTemplateRows`). The removed props are silently ignored at\n  runtime, so without this every custom preview and input would lose its\n  spacing and grid layout.\n- @sanity/ui v4 types only allow valid DOM attributes. Drop the\n  `width=\"fill\"` (Flex) and `rows` (Stack) props, which never did\n  anything, and render the distribution input labels as <label> so\n  `htmlFor` is valid.\n- @sanity/icons v5 no longer exports icons from the package root. The\n  Studio build failed on TrashIcon/AddIcon/SearchIcon, so import them\n  from their subpaths instead.\n- Remove an unused deep import of\n  sanity/src/core/components/previews/_common/Media, which is not part\n  of the public API.\n- Update studio/tsconfig.json to use bundler module resolution and\n  skipLibCheck. @sanity/ui v4 resolves its types through package\n  exports, so the old node10 resolution could not find them.\n\nNothing else in the Sanity v5/v6 migration notes applies here: there is\nno auth.mode, enableLegacySearch or custom Vite config, and Node 22.x\nalready meets the new >= 22.12 requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fecc3e40667104b4f5fe2c1b449d1c5cbb16b108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/fecc3e40667104b4f5fe2c1b449d1c5cbb16b108"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07","verification":{"payload":"tree fecc3e40667104b4f5fe2c1b449d1c5cbb16b108\nparent d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790946532 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790946532 +0200\n\nUpgrade Sanity Studio to v6 and React 19 (#1173)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Sanity Studio to v6 and React 19\n\nBump the Studio in studio/ to the current majors:\n- sanity and @sanity/vision 4.22 -> 6.17\n- react / react-dom 18.3 -> 19.3 (Studio v5+ requires React >= 19.2)\n- @sanity/ui 3.5 -> 4.3, @sanity/table 1.1 -> 3.1\n- add @sanity/icons ^5.2 as an explicit dependency, since our custom\n  inputs import from it directly\n\nBreaking changes handled:\n- @sanity/ui v4 removed the deprecated `space` prop (now `gap`) and the\n  Grid `columns` / `rows` props (now `gridTemplateColumns` /\n  `gridTemplateRows`). The removed props are silently ignored at\n  runtime, so without this every custom preview and input would lose its\n  spacing and grid layout.\n- @sanity/ui v4 types only allow valid DOM attributes. Drop the\n  `width=\"fill\"` (Flex) and `rows` (Stack) props, which never did\n  anything, and render the distribution input labels as <label> so\n  `htmlFor` is valid.\n- @sanity/icons v5 no longer exports icons from the package root. The\n  Studio build failed on TrashIcon/AddIcon/SearchIcon, so import them\n  from their subpaths instead.\n- Remove an unused deep import of\n  sanity/src/core/components/previews/_common/Media, which is not part\n  of the public API.\n- Update studio/tsconfig.json to use bundler module resolution and\n  skipLibCheck. @sanity/ui v4 resolves its types through package\n  exports, so the old node10 resolution could not find them.\n\nNothing else in the Sanity v5/v6 migration notes applies here: there is\nno auth.mode, enableLegacySearch or custom Vite config, and Node 22.x\nalready meets the new >= 22.12 requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv6zkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMpoQADmUhxQ9yFK9Z3rY5SBSCVKs\nIBsX3QIXy/3kjCPyMGUzbxE7j+LM9X7UiXtziiRSTGwU0QskiqeBmZGlxDpEZTZO\nCSwwT+RJacOO7siKZBOPn1f11fAOHovObxMxjG4k+aaz7LhoGSjGzxLdhjDsjZ1K\nSUYWeXEMj1M0zFVDavEhUDkRO9nWHkg9Cz3AJsk37XsuqVLMJn+g7Ri8Ie8oKSiy\nrQVy9UjYw2U9hzMo89FWY8DMPGM6hlnF4Jb2aJ23qFThOsAUEkNavwVtd+WRuzAn\nOPSgUzMnNx6Pi0Mc8ZP1knwESf+HQmY3p8WZJDitxk86EtmcCrvVImTB2ODx9ZFs\nLzr6rOMrSBHtRZ9eh7a3aBiBr2Cbi/Gvt8BTck1k2xUbmFXff0Z9kQQ4ej7uNkUC\n10vaTRKjHEBB3GxbgZF4ooy4Hps4qGab/UqkWqlGeJGQ5GAQKJZSeeKtVubYvxwq\ngYs4fYcBujhksAxxwVltzt99XyGRQTLSunwN3whn6AJs6D70MP1RRc1CP4fpOHH5\nIpiKppwZ6LPR9j+eAvGVFUFOjmw9fSH+ylL6T80FeVLu57TWtkm9Fj5mfs4S6yvD\n2ldY59DLGtUogDnJgXCU5xB1ubDeoLPZXgnzDQwbfnhFj6sO/1LxUQLJKEnRJS7n\nJOcG914e34p41mqRb40E\n=plc+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:08:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGE0ZDNlM2EzMzFhNDAwYjE2MzgyMzIyYWFhYjI5MDJlM2FjNjFjMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149","sha":"d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149"}],"sha":"a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a4d3e3a331a400b16382322aaab2902e3ac61c07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:05:38Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T13:05:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade @auth0/auth0-react to 2.28 and handle missing access tokens (#1168)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade @auth0/auth0-react to 2.28.1 and guard against missing access tokens\n\nFrom 2.25, getAccessTokenSilently() is typed Promise<string | undefined>.\nThat is not only a typing change. Since auth0-spa-js 2.22 the SDK enforces\nthe IPSIE `session_expiry` ceiling: once it has passed, it clears the local\nsession and resolves with undefined rather than throwing. Previously we\nwould then have called the API with \"Bearer undefined\".\n\n- hooks/useApi.ts: derive the getAccessTokenSilently type from\n  Auth0ContextInterface instead of copying the library''s overloads by hand\n  (that copy is what broke). Add getAccessToken(), which throws a\n  MissingAccessTokenError when no token comes back.\n- Use getAccessToken() in the SWR fetcher (_queries.ts) and at every\n  direct token call site in components/profile/*. When the session has\n  expired, Auth0Provider clears `user`, and UserWrapper then redirects to\n  login as before.\n\nuser.sub is not used anywhere. Donor IDs come from the custom claim via\ngetUserId(), so the user.sub type change needs no code change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a9d6fb19d4d651351a5d778bfc66fd465e465f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/2a9d6fb19d4d651351a5d778bfc66fd465e465f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a9d6fb19d4d651351a5d778bfc66fd465e465f1\nparent d1e0ff44a0b3a51982643d794f118a9b81d2d60b\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790946338 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790946338 +0200\n\nUpgrade @auth0/auth0-react to 2.28 and handle missing access tokens (#1168)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade @auth0/auth0-react to 2.28.1 and guard against missing access tokens\n\nFrom 2.25, getAccessTokenSilently() is typed Promise<string | undefined>.\nThat is not only a typing change. Since auth0-spa-js 2.22 the SDK enforces\nthe IPSIE `session_expiry` ceiling: once it has passed, it clears the local\nsession and resolves with undefined rather than throwing. Previously we\nwould then have called the API with \"Bearer undefined\".\n\n- hooks/useApi.ts: derive the getAccessTokenSilently type from\n  Auth0ContextInterface instead of copying the library''s overloads by hand\n  (that copy is what broke). Add getAccessToken(), which throws a\n  MissingAccessTokenError when no token comes back.\n- Use getAccessToken() in the SWR fetcher (_queries.ts) and at every\n  direct token call site in components/profile/*. When the session has\n  expired, Auth0Provider clears `user`, and UserWrapper then redirects to\n  login as before.\n\nuser.sub is not used anywhere. Donor IDs come from the custom claim via\ngetUserId(), so the user.sub type change needs no code change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv6wiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAa1AQAH4Zn2+k3wEmcJWeVESkT7FW\niD/1QcFfDsqfjS8F9Yi3iZTwy2VP1yJFcCNyFlbRwFnItEfQAseK9eeqpK3rk93w\ncvxWa0drCjnV0lWG4g7rit2O0myeJiZBcOImN9tjB8UXCuWBAXVN6yywNWsRK3/t\n+gMcVU+FBYsAgzvZW2rwtRE+27gY3EtRQKgTKVc+/o2PEsZWmBvMYyyCphVgqYXQ\n0EqyVC9bdMTgNROCdBzdyAXzNratZPNY/6De3xRNZk4ybKhP8onisFkL17e6i3P2\nf4xjYClLSszo61M473TsY4Uq/rW5gFtvjkowmvz4/oxXTGu551PrijwE6CifwLG1\nI+UEVVuvMvWIH8QvG8/krLDVKrpfpPy9sXxpyU7jZoZkpS5kt1ZidSUPRT6dbAVu\nTxkETOsEjz+rVtTAMobAyEziespK645bGeDVHyTizyNe0hHK7I0jPxpHAIHc/CvK\nCdabVH7dui9zn/4XDsxOMbOw8QLSI/aJ1d8F34FJedlYlGgQMl0xqwBfgr1G9af5\nsx4d05iT/3pXJX4i39i7+BiBSwZHbcNaPoOQWxGyxDnTD3rwkHDW35DAtvUNDzlh\n1tbK5vjoFaromDcStx1qGamZ8aca9bL0g1kDKcZuioWoFHpN7+HgXQ0Vt9342+Zp\ne1X0AP1wIWdLd4HPyGg8\n=sDrg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T13:05:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGQyY2NhMTcwNDE1MjlkNDEwNGQyMzM0NmEzNDIwY2NmMjNlZGExNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/d1e0ff44a0b3a51982643d794f118a9b81d2d60b","sha":"d1e0ff44a0b3a51982643d794f118a9b81d2d60b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/d1e0ff44a0b3a51982643d794f118a9b81d2d60b"}],"sha":"d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/d2cca17041529d4104d23346a3420ccf23eda149"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/d1e0ff44a0b3a51982643d794f118a9b81d2d60b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:51:13Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:51:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade next-sanity to 13, @sanity/client to 8, visual-editing to 6, image-url to 2 (#1174)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Sanity frontend libraries to next-sanity 13 / @sanity/client 8\n\nBump next-sanity 12 -> 13, @sanity/client 7 -> 8, @sanity/visual-editing\n5 -> 6 and @sanity/image-url 1 -> 2 in the root app (studio/ is untouched).\n\nBreaking changes handled:\n- @sanity/image-url 2 removed the lib/types/types deep import; types are\n  now exported from the package root, so all SanityImageObject/SanityAsset\n  imports use `import type { ... } from \"@sanity/image-url\"`.\n- next-sanity 13''s <VisualEditing> now wires in App Router server actions\n  (next/headers cookies + refresh), which do not work in the Pages Router.\n  _app now uses @sanity/visual-editing/next-pages-router, the documented\n  Pages Router integration.\n- @sanity/preview-kit (latest 6.2.0) still depends on @sanity/client 7,\n  so its SanityClient type is nominally incompatible with v8. It only uses\n  config/withConfig/fetch/live.events, which v8 keeps, so PreviewProvider\n  casts at that one boundary.\n- next-sanity no longer needs transpilePackages: the remaining extensionless\n  \"next/dynamic\" imports in 13 are only in next-sanity/live and\n  next-sanity/visual-editing, neither of which we import any more.\n\nnpm audit: next-sanity pulls in `sanity` (now 6.x) as an auto-installed\npeer, whose CLI tooling pins vulnerable transitive versions with no fixed\nupstream release yet. Add scoped overrides to patched versions of the same\nAPIs: @module-federation/dts-plugin 2.9.2 (adm-zip 0.6.1, undici 7.29.1),\njs-yaml 3.15.2 and smol-toml 1.9 under @vercel/frameworks, and uuid 11\nunder typeid-js (it only uses v7/stringify). None of this code runs in the\nNext app. Root advisories go from 13 to 4 (remaining: csv-parse,\nlint-staged/micromatch/yaml, handled separately).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop stale nested lockfile entries so the audit overrides apply\n\nnpm kept js-yaml@3.13.1 under @vercel/frameworks and uuid@10 under\ntypeid-js as \"invalid: overridden\" instead of replacing them, so the\noverrides added for the Sanity CLI advisories never took effect.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"631593f45a701b444aac276a441ed5a140115bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/631593f45a701b444aac276a441ed5a140115bf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/d1e0ff44a0b3a51982643d794f118a9b81d2d60b","verification":{"payload":"tree 631593f45a701b444aac276a441ed5a140115bf6\nparent 35f10423e631c85cb18039e857fd6db9aaa2a440\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790945473 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790945473 +0200\n\nUpgrade next-sanity to 13, @sanity/client to 8, visual-editing to 6, image-url to 2 (#1174)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Sanity frontend libraries to next-sanity 13 / @sanity/client 8\n\nBump next-sanity 12 -> 13, @sanity/client 7 -> 8, @sanity/visual-editing\n5 -> 6 and @sanity/image-url 1 -> 2 in the root app (studio/ is untouched).\n\nBreaking changes handled:\n- @sanity/image-url 2 removed the lib/types/types deep import; types are\n  now exported from the package root, so all SanityImageObject/SanityAsset\n  imports use `import type { ... } from \"@sanity/image-url\"`.\n- next-sanity 13''s <VisualEditing> now wires in App Router server actions\n  (next/headers cookies + refresh), which do not work in the Pages Router.\n  _app now uses @sanity/visual-editing/next-pages-router, the documented\n  Pages Router integration.\n- @sanity/preview-kit (latest 6.2.0) still depends on @sanity/client 7,\n  so its SanityClient type is nominally incompatible with v8. It only uses\n  config/withConfig/fetch/live.events, which v8 keeps, so PreviewProvider\n  casts at that one boundary.\n- next-sanity no longer needs transpilePackages: the remaining extensionless\n  \"next/dynamic\" imports in 13 are only in next-sanity/live and\n  next-sanity/visual-editing, neither of which we import any more.\n\nnpm audit: next-sanity pulls in `sanity` (now 6.x) as an auto-installed\npeer, whose CLI tooling pins vulnerable transitive versions with no fixed\nupstream release yet. Add scoped overrides to patched versions of the same\nAPIs: @module-federation/dts-plugin 2.9.2 (adm-zip 0.6.1, undici 7.29.1),\njs-yaml 3.15.2 and smol-toml 1.9 under @vercel/frameworks, and uuid 11\nunder typeid-js (it only uses v7/stringify). None of this code runs in the\nNext app. Root advisories go from 13 to 4 (remaining: csv-parse,\nlint-staged/micromatch/yaml, handled separately).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop stale nested lockfile entries so the audit overrides apply\n\nnpm kept js-yaml@3.13.1 under @vercel/frameworks and uuid@10 under\ntypeid-js as \"invalid: overridden\" instead of replacing them, so the\noverrides added for the Sanity CLI advisories never took effect.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv6jBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKdAQADVkLT47JEFJIfAAhZODFpoB\nVclVTOuDD6uaSbhz703PDfpOpoMR5ZMnDUdLs5cIt/H+nQ3r+vOoxRt0OfDA9N0f\nYkph5Zr/P6lpvW5H58LmP0Ew+RIx9u3Fvgen+IzglHVFbsr3+9pHE2nTYnCAesBO\nuoPpTq+yhizw9QKRBUTD8kF3ipan6gpYi4MB+HouCL+2F9rNCS9bxTsLRv8CmYNi\n/GmIUGCkmo1i6weQK5w2MEv2pobrrM/dl4yr3FW+b6o9u6O6Ws1l1ncd6OfHdnrq\nobmUXF+vbkb+U+XDaAZYlq2uhLdk17LmkmYvZPuasfE9tVXZU+7dG6YqvlcTBATF\nuPQou5qi7SjWz5EPxAmfUV22fdzpE/b4jiy5hCuBfi8oyzNbhfdKCVDyv2sM+SpW\ntf25EQNUL5/pGV41Dp1k4nydY39nNry/RujJhxRAYyR+bMmc/szXpQaxxoIjY4+c\nh