-effekt/main-site/commit/e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4","sha":"e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4"}],"sha":"0b7bd8dce346543f38abda1f93c41364a0271249","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/0b7bd8dce346543f38abda1f93c41364a0271249"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:02:55Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T12:02:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade Jest to 30 and Cypress to 16; remove unused loaders (#1175)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Jest to 30\n\nBump jest and babel-jest to 30.5.2 and @types/jest to 30.0.0. ts-jest\nstays on 29.4.14, which is the latest release and already declares\nJest 30 as a supported peer.\n\nNone of the matcher aliases removed in Jest 30 (toBeCalled, toThrowError,\netc.) are used in our tests, and we use the node test environment, so no\ntest changes were needed. The jest.config.js JSDoc type is switched from\nthe deprecated ts-jest/dist/types InitialOptionsTsJest to the public\nJestConfigWithTsJest export.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Cypress to 16 and its plugins\n\nBump cypress 15.21 -> 16.1, cypress-dotenv 2 -> 3, cypress-fail-fast\n7 -> 8 and cypress-localstorage-commands 1 -> 2 (the plugin versions that\nsupport Cypress 16).\n\nCypress 16 removes Cypress.env(), so the login command and the profile\nspec now read the Auth0 test credentials via cy.env(), which still picks\nup the CYPRESS_* variables from CI and from .env.local via cypress-dotenv.\ncypress-fail-fast 8 reads its settings through Cypress.expose() with\ncamelCase keys, so the SE config moves FAIL_FAST_ENABLED/STRATEGY from\n`env` to `expose.failFastEnabled/failFastStrategy`.\n\nCypress 16 also switches to a visibility check based on\nElement.checkVisibility(), which does not treat elements translated off\nscreen as hidden. The navbar test now asserts the navbar is scrolled\nabove the viewport instead of \"not.be.visible\", and the fundraiser\nclickUntilVisible helper only re-clicks while the start button is still\nvisible (it could otherwise try to click the already-hidden button).\n\nThe e2e workflow moves to cypress-io/github-action@v7 (v6 runs on the\ndeprecated node20 runtime) and installs Node from .nvmrc, since Cypress\n16 requires Node 22/24.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove unused babel-loader and sass-loader\n\nNeither package is referenced anywhere: there is no webpack config,\nStorybook or custom loader setup, the app builds with Turbopack, Next\ncompiles SCSS with its own bundled sass integration (only `sass` is\nneeded), and Jest transforms with ts-jest. Removing them instead of\nupgrading to babel-loader 10 / sass-loader 17 also drops their webpack\npeer dependency tree from the lockfile.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7176e96821faedf4647ac96b2ad35a1efa7cc2c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/7176e96821faedf4647ac96b2ad35a1efa7cc2c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4","verification":{"payload":"tree 7176e96821faedf4647ac96b2ad35a1efa7cc2c0\nparent 1492a93a9a05cf9f7db3e179d56e7ecf1c8251d7\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790942575 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790942575 +0200\n\nUpgrade Jest to 30 and Cypress to 16; remove unused loaders (#1175)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Jest to 30\n\nBump jest and babel-jest to 30.5.2 and @types/jest to 30.0.0. ts-jest\nstays on 29.4.14, which is the latest release and already declares\nJest 30 as a supported peer.\n\nNone of the matcher aliases removed in Jest 30 (toBeCalled, toThrowError,\netc.) are used in our tests, and we use the node test environment, so no\ntest changes were needed. The jest.config.js JSDoc type is switched from\nthe deprecated ts-jest/dist/types InitialOptionsTsJest to the public\nJestConfigWithTsJest export.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade Cypress to 16 and its plugins\n\nBump cypress 15.21 -> 16.1, cypress-dotenv 2 -> 3, cypress-fail-fast\n7 -> 8 and cypress-localstorage-commands 1 -> 2 (the plugin versions that\nsupport Cypress 16).\n\nCypress 16 removes Cypress.env(), so the login command and the profile\nspec now read the Auth0 test credentials via cy.env(), which still picks\nup the CYPRESS_* variables from CI and from .env.local via cypress-dotenv.\ncypress-fail-fast 8 reads its settings through Cypress.expose() with\ncamelCase keys, so the SE config moves FAIL_FAST_ENABLED/STRATEGY from\n`env` to `expose.failFastEnabled/failFastStrategy`.\n\nCypress 16 also switches to a visibility check based on\nElement.checkVisibility(), which does not treat elements translated off\nscreen as hidden. The navbar test now asserts the navbar is scrolled\nabove the viewport instead of \"not.be.visible\", and the fundraiser\nclickUntilVisible helper only re-clicks while the start button is still\nvisible (it could otherwise try to click the already-hidden button).\n\nThe e2e workflow moves to cypress-io/github-action@v7 (v6 runs on the\ndeprecated node20 runtime) and installs Node from .nvmrc, since Cypress\n16 requires Node 22/24.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove unused babel-loader and sass-loader\n\nNeither package is referenced anywhere: there is no webpack config,\nStorybook or custom loader setup, the app builds with Turbopack, Next\ncompiles SCSS with its own bundled sass integration (only `sass` is\nneeded), and Jest transforms with ts-jest. Removing them instead of\nupgrading to babel-loader 10 / sass-loader 17 also drops their webpack\npeer dependency tree from the lockfile.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv51vCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2mAQAClzMIrnlb6c6eoWmpB3sZ7y\nfO5iwXBX48M6gU0mNcTkN/UCNP72XV62cyVcpYniy2nDHTAierMrOHsQQnQq+DK5\nALbzu1fT6aPPrAfVNg8ATvnZYpgpBkxCrfxvEu1brQorYGI5PWM31G5at6ZC28UA\nvGekw5AAV0cCKZMYVlnh26ECVTFNhSA25C4nmWdn/E5pO2OEfPonQkxTLe4B+lmm\nZyuux7N2g7z0v8pHX3Qzme8K+Z0iudFeEv/widvjLb6upJ9+90O/LJaZ79gd1v/X\nUp1MZuQUGRSGYsKWDOCkyr6rFqLzGSTrcN2eDO1QdumMAMslTu3hZq1YdFhaPkop\n3xv6XgaSweTs6ACy3kZQslz7/De1c0iJf8kycjLULrViOaoK3brLE8SvpkJOxF6G\no9cbFZolZxH0DIg5sU9vC5BQfPIh95crflpYQW0fx0LBXhDgqQ+XnUq2dp4vmkiU\nTejBlWBRXVa+nhFct7S0FRCPzwwpodFlGlIEyvMzvvLIvsbind/GCFi4Ac+ndvHd\nYbslJQ00dJuW3DK0yuT7uGMa7Fazv5x1mKY1zQJmWLhYJFoC6pb8wVclnPtIydYD\nz6yKYKldiAGpmJRrGQNhxDRV9ZOtBajPCkqke/gTsrtpvM6kOYhFbF+Nzfih5Nla\nd+5jqXQJnRF5dLGUqm0c\n=pFY4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T12:02:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGU3NzQwYmM5NTVhMjRmMjMxYTk1OTg1NTBjZWJhNmE4NjI2NGExZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/1492a93a9a05cf9f7db3e179d56e7ecf1c8251d7","sha":"1492a93a9a05cf9f7db3e179d56e7ecf1c8251d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/1492a93a9a05cf9f7db3e179d56e7ecf1c8251d7"}],"sha":"e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/e7740bc955a24f231a9598550ceba6a86264a1e4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/1492a93a9a05cf9f7db3e179d56e7ecf1c8251d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:54:50Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:54:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade @portabletext/react from 3.2 to 8.0 (#1169)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade @portabletext/react from 3.2 to 8.0\n\nMoves the rich text renderer to the current major so we stay on a\nmaintained release line. None of the breaking changes between 3 and 8\nneed code changes here:\n\n- v4/v7: requires React 19 (we are on 19.3).\n- v5: ESM-only and Node >= 20.19. Next bundles it without needing\n  transpilePackages, and Jest does not import any PortableText module.\n- v6: @portabletext/types v4 (string literal unions). We use untyped\n  component overrides, so no type changes.\n- v7: ships a React Compiler build by default; no API changes.\n- v8: Node >= 22.12 (Vercel projects use 22.x), and lists now nest as\n  deeply as their `level`. That only affects lists that start below\n  level 1 or skip levels; none of the checked pages render differently.\n\nnext-sanity still brings its own nested @portabletext/react, which the\ncomponents importing PortableText from next-sanity keep using.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f33a5fe2f0bde564c7839be500d2941067317136","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/f33a5fe2f0bde564c7839be500d2941067317136"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/1492a93a9a05cf9f7db3e179d56e7ecf1c8251d7","verification":{"payload":"tree f33a5fe2f0bde564c7839be500d2941067317136\nparent 65a039e4b7e7bba4c6aa4d796a09576b5b0435fb\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790942090 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790942090 +0200\n\nUpgrade @portabletext/react from 3.2 to 8.0 (#1169)\n\n* Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Upgrade @portabletext/react from 3.2 to 8.0\n\nMoves the rich text renderer to the current major so we stay on a\nmaintained release line. None of the breaking changes between 3 and 8\nneed code changes here:\n\n- v4/v7: requires React 19 (we are on 19.3).\n- v5: ESM-only and Node >= 20.19. Next bundles it without needing\n  transpilePackages, and Jest does not import any PortableText module.\n- v6: @portabletext/types v4 (string literal unions). We use untyped\n  component overrides, so no type changes.\n- v7: ships a React Compiler build by default; no API changes.\n- v8: Node >= 22.12 (Vercel projects use 22.x), and lists now nest as\n  deeply as their `level`. That only affects lists that start below\n  level 1 or skip levels; none of the checked pages render differently.\n\nnext-sanity still brings its own nested @portabletext/react, which the\ncomponents importing PortableText from next-sanity keep using.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv5uKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA150QAI6oIZdJHVPsL8SFgu2tRKvr\nfxeD5QBBa9e4YoeDKEvKjo8gcA4gdl9sRKjS8NLyECJVtG7MHzz5c+1uY0PJLtK3\nv0xlyRJ6PQIekuW4wsUothp7w7mKYc35SrFvJLxTKh0PLwhQEsRaUz6jT4ey4JSL\nhrfQzCCHZ46e98knTezJBDZuEjkYRCUdt1jWGpCCsEAEiSiuix4Kd6NE5Cpu1dXD\n+aKP9lTLtEWej/qo7q6kUxiJmcNscXci9PyZAbSxtBeOLAtpntxcKUSA8jNOApKX\nM8N9upKRiyjV/FJ0XuETRQUtBlX7N9AL4o1thSllIxIxyYrNixwiqC2T5ABWZr0s\neZoiuq02qTOTeTAFxqYkUmQ3sw6qdtu19UT/IHLUn2oyjR6sz+RxEpnlQfXMDJkP\nf5QI/YYGaCh+wG81+1pM54PCD50g9CW13b/WRWbvHBXKxU8eaNbV0BFimoNKO29o\noGF/llEgFtvot/4E6uOFXV2Wpwq73nW8AB4+d8DVWvNa1pFYr7zwo00liWTD4ESs\nEtIz7D4cwnCRaAdF6tBbRZf9WMzX+DdvcZIMq6WyOzbnJVISBpf1wZwHH6fKPTZG\n11BgdVdHleoGh8ttJAoBqleF+V8tXeCzuMGEZ6QoX/Wt0V+rWN0R+AXGUjd2ZCRX\njZK2eX7Us0skbnMIRqJL\n=VZ2U\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T11:54:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.gith