users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/65a039e4b7e7bba4c6aa4d796a09576b5b0435fb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:44:20Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T11:44:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Bump dependencies within their current semver ranges (#1167)\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb64555eb42acaf6c27227cf3280e2bd2e154003","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/cb64555eb42acaf6c27227cf3280e2bd2e154003"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/65a039e4b7e7bba4c6aa4d796a09576b5b0435fb","verification":{"payload":"tree cb64555eb42acaf6c27227cf3280e2bd2e154003\nparent a2f75408485d1825547ae6bd3e8b53a83b3df741\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790941460 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790941460 +0200\n\nBump dependencies within their current semver ranges (#1167)\n\nRun `npm update --save` and `npm audit fix` in the root and studio.\nRoot advisories drop from 51 to 13 and studio from 46 to 12, clearing\nboth criticals (tar and decompress in the Sanity CLI). Everything left\nneeds a major bump.\n\n- Transpile next-sanity: 12.4 imports \"next/dynamic\" without an\n  extension, which fails when loaded as an external ESM module.\n- Keep @auth0/auth0-react on 2.10: 2.25+ types getAccessTokenSilently\n  as possibly undefined, which needs code changes (separate PR).\n- Pin the @types/react override to the direct dependency''s range.\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv5kUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMhUQAJbXEwcCYBoBjPojfcJz9wad\nLCm2uGv/CaKEiAfDFqbEvm9hL7vERcpozIf8ZX1tzaPTR2n5bgJDjAwBPhICOeLj\nLlfZuBRd41pPyozR4CLMw7FXO1wfrxjnIHiaNmdcfkDMtsE7o2JtIX+6sVVbj7yA\nxHPVspC2fVzJmvnB2ADdgvSXbasCuxKgTP5znst+kiEfmCJFwL+TSnfGGbDSIHcg\nsYHRg+3IyhmgTlzkrYynj+hqkABBm6NaziF8hKvCiogBSSmVfR1pjpzaNAc9dTYt\naUXeqYrljfFiVGID/T7rdzvPK8L4ePRn4kkKC4B/ZFSt3u8LeGcd0YybHV93oAsX\ncK2PdJAQU9dqqVKS8dLzNGO9mgmGR+QU6oBbJREP8M8b6qggYUBjXTzfbzhC+AMR\nke0uDO5rp6a3EmoJuKkDlKDvjV7fTDGC0cJcyAHbEcG37cn3vwwPKap7W5NsdY0i\nl5D9exB525YlDSIwS8uShy/PgIaLltD4gvTUda8ebZ/ic2FJ1Z0byfTgZ0A4KuUw\nq9xB2FLy+cdXdb5l3YxDHXwwAERwiK3TaEYFf9MYW9tnfld0Y06RnRYHkmSYA4b4\nwdlqtAlopCivRU4GgG7+4Kk5+Woa19IxLB+Oeykz9JSgKZ1jtJq2yeQ20gXVV/c/\nhC4TbKpEdnU6XOwjElbD\n=MP96\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-02T11:44:20Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/65a039e4b7e7bba4c6aa4d796a09576b5b0435fb","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKDY1YTAzOWU0YjdlN2JiYTRjNmFhNGQ3OTZhMDk1NzZiNWIwNDM1ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/a2f75408485d1825547ae6bd3e8b53a83b3df741","sha":"a2f75408485d1825547ae6bd3e8b53a83b3df741","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a2f75408485d1825547ae6bd3e8b53a83b3df741"}],"sha":"65a039e4b7e7bba4c6aa4d796a09576b5b0435fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/65a039e4b7e7bba4c6aa4d796a09576b5b0435fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/693641?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fellmirr","id":693641,"login":"fellmirr","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MzY0MQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fellmirr","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/a2f75408485d1825547ae6bd3e8b53a83b3df741/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:38:46Z","email":"account@harnes.me","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T10:38:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Upgrade Next.js to 16.3.8 and remove logo full-navigation workaround (#1165)\n\n* Upgrade Next.js to 16.3.8 and remove logo full-navigation workaround\n\nLinks to \"/\" (e.g. the navbar logo) rendered a plain <a> to force a full\npage load, working around a client-side navigation crash from Next 14.\nThat crash no longer reproduces, so route them through next/link again.\n\nNext 16.3 now fails the build on type errors in Jest test files, caused\nby Cypress''s Chai `expect` types leaking into the root program. Give\nCypress its own tsconfig and exclude it from the root one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop empty slug segments in getStaticPaths\n\nThe frontpage slug \"/\" split into [\"\", \"\"], generating \"/accepted/\" etc.\nVercel''s Next.js adapter (used from Next 16.2+) emits that as\n\"accepted/.func\", and the deploy step then fails with\nENOENT readlink ''functions/accepted.func''.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbe2a5e9f585b9d944abeb1cb8e9b49199227851","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/bbe2a5e9f585b9d944abeb1cb8e9b49199227851"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/a2f75408485d1825547ae6bd3e8b53a83b3df741","verification":{"payload":"tree bbe2a5e9f585b9d944abeb1cb8e9b49199227851\nparent 15130c4e38cc300536e010203382de1d82ca4882\nauthor Håkon Harnes <account@harnes.me> 1790937526 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790937526 +0200\n\nUpgrade Next.js to 16.3.8 and remove logo full-navigation workaround (#1165)\n\n* Upgrade Next.js to 16.3.8 and remove logo full-navigation workaround\n\nLinks to \"/\" (e.g. the navbar logo) rendered a plain <a> to force a full\npage load, working around a client-side navigation crash from Next 14.\nThat crash no longer reproduces, so route them through next/link again.\n\nNext 16.3 now fails the build on type errors in Jest test files, caused\nby Cypress''s Chai `expect` types leaking into the root program. Give\nCypress its own tsconfig and exclude it from the root one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Drop empty slug segments in getStaticPaths\n\nThe frontpage slug \"/\" split into [\"\", \"\"], generating \"/accepted/\" etc.\nVercel''s Next.js adapter (used from Next 16.2+) emits that as\n\"accepted/.func\", and the deploy step then fails with\nENOENT readlink ''functions/accepted.func''.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Håkon Harnes <hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqv4m2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA2JwQAAU9GMpdJ9VE33sHgsrCP9mW\nX6gOEpaT5sym3YV9wrZnN3XOvCEdoWpzqPtv/dXjb+DBnJdz7EnbKjLaqPXRHWjC\nFlUIutH+LRZbEmc9/TU5TzK2eSPRnFThihamfSbsA7tEgmdn+jUIhwUx6Q5uRE1m\neirPmSOCMCdg2sSu/R9Nd3lk93QxzJWq2Eofl8gu0OGzOaqJ6NSzWxP3r7irhvGS\njeqW3gK1e0qCIUoKeB1YYYthzc6A50GJTTChhDjwRF6YhtJdPRl1W8CtmLLfB0/W\nzCy8IGcASf9Na6hkzi1NmTPJT0Z64z9MldhqHrAHlr5MH3YFEdozv1RJuQaVZoTM\n2mimf4gcK54Wi7wHzaEwQk+kxN0lTP780q+1