9","sha":"41d534a6acc6aa7a19bf2b32d4aa64f6459d2d09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/41d534a6acc6aa7a19bf2b32d4aa64f6459d2d09"}],"sha":"754e465d2ef95f5d1fe0f9d89e34745478d426d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/754e465d2ef95f5d1fe0f9d89e34745478d426d9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/c701556eee83e33c7d4e2c504243fd8e97e6e859/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T20:08:01Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T20:08:01Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"message":"Make SE e2e widget setup wait for hydration instead of a fixed delay\n\nsetupWidgetTest clicked the give button after a flat cy.wait(500). Under CI load that\nclick can land before React hydrates, so it is silently dropped and the widget never\nopens - surfacing much later as a confusing \"widget pane has display: none\" failure on\nwhichever cause-area click came next. Which test failed therefore varied between runs.\n\nNow it waits on the cause-areas request (client-side only, so it implies hydration) and\nasserts the pane actually opened, which both removes the race and makes a lost click\nfail at the point it happens. Also moves the .as() alias onto the intercept rather than\nthe fixture, so it is actually waitable.","tree":{"sha":"5ac978b9d00c2b3d081adff2f6085bc04781da4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/5ac978b9d00c2b3d081adff2f6085bc04781da4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/c701556eee83e33c7d4e2c504243fd8e97e6e859","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/c701556eee83e33c7d4e2c504243fd8e97e6e859","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGM3MDE1NTZlZWU4M2UzM2M3ZDRlMmM1MDQyNDNmZDhlOTdlNmU4NTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5","sha":"fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5"}],"sha":"c701556eee83e33c7d4e2c504243fd8e97e6e859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/c701556eee83e33c7d4e2c504243fd8e97e6e859"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:46:29Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:46:29Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"message":"Force hidden-checkbox interactions in SE e2e specs\n\nThe operations cut checkboxes are visually-hidden inputs behind styled labels inside\na position:fixed widget pane, so an unforced check()/uncheck() passes or fails purely\non scroll position - it passed locally and failed in CI.","tree":{"sha":"c59a72b2a1066bf5c4d2b8972466728866d8401c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/c59a72b2a1066bf5c4d2b8972466728866d8401c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGZhMTEyZmE1ZWE5M2M0OWYwODA4ZjhjOGNjNWZjMTgyNWJhN2U5YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f","sha":"949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f"}],"sha":"fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/fa112fa5ea93c49f0808f8c8cc5fc1825ba7e9b5"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:37:29Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:37:29Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"message":"Drop last hardcoded English label fallback in the amount pane\n\napplyWidgetDefaults always populates ui_labels and every platform now configures\ntotal_label in Sanity, so the \"Total\" fallback could only ever mask missing content.","tree":{"sha":"1cf9d2021eabfcf687bf19b955059825b03d1452","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/1cf9d2021eabfcf687bf19b955059825b03d1452"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKDk0OWIzOGRiMzFkMTNjOTc2ZTA1MGNhZjAzZDg5ZGIxYTEwZjk4MmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b","sha":"b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b"}],"sha":"949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/949b38db31d13c976e050caf03d89db1a10f982f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:36:31Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T19:36:31Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"message":"Make info-box links CMS-configured, fix payment-button dead-end, green SE e2e\n\nInfo box links were hardcoded: OperationsCauseAreaForm pointed the X-faktor box at\na literal https://giveffektivt.dk/x-faktor from shared widget code, so the link was\nwrong on every platform except Denmark and unchangeable without a deploy. Both info\nboxes (x_factor_info and other_cause_area_info) now take an optional `link` as a\nSanity navitem - the same internal-page reference type privacy_policy_link already\nuses - resolved to a slug in the widget query. Populated DK''s X-faktor box with copy\nthat states the ~7x figure and a navitem pointing at its existing x-faktor page,\nresolved by slug rather than a hardcoded document ID.\n\nFix a real dead-end in DonorPane: the payment controls were disabled whenever\n`errors` was non-empty, but because submission validates via trigger() rather than\nhandleSubmit(), react-hook-form never marks the form submitted and so never\nre-validates on change. A donor who submitted once with a bad email was left with\npermanently disabled payment buttons even after correcting it. Submission is still\ngated - handlePayment awaits trigger() and bails on invalid input - so dropping the\ndisabled state loses no protection.\n\nAlso disable the global operations percentage input when the global cut is off,\nmatching the per-cause-area input, and add per-cause-area data-cy attributes to the\ndistribution radios so tests can target them without ambiguous text matching.\n\nSE e2e is now fully green (100/100). The remaining failures were a mix of stale\nexpectations and genuinely wrong test data: assertions still expecting the English\n\"Operations\"/\"Smart distribution\" that Sanity now localizes, org percentages\nexpected as shares of the grand total rather than within their cause area, autogiro\nsubmit tests that never switched to recurring (autogiro is recurring-only), a\npersonnummer that fails its check digit, and a state-persistence test asserting\namounts are cleared when switching selection - the reducer deliberately preserves\nthem, so the test now documents that intent instead.","tree":{"sha":"1adfd1dddb77fbe3f49a1e208e3a545897d3e2fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/1adfd1dddb77fbe3f49a1e208e3a545897d3e2fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKGI3YzRmNDA1NzIxNDY5YWExMDExNzA4MjczNTIwYzJhYTNhOWFiMmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25","sha":"8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25"}],"sha":"b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/b7c4f405721469aa1011708273520c2aa3a9ab2b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-24T18:39:02Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-24T18:39:02Z","email":"hakon.harnes@effektiv-spenden.org","name":"Håkon Harnes"},"message":"Source all widget copy from Sanity per platform, make cause area IDs configurable\n\nEvery user-facing string in the widget now comes from Sanity per platform, so\nnothing falls back to an English default on a Nordic site. Concretely:\n\n- Remove the hardcoded `locale === \"dk\"` copy override block in Widget.tsx that\n  injected Danish strings at runtime.\n- Add two missing Sanity fields for strings that were hardcoded in components:\n  smart_distribution_context.show_all_organizations_text (was \"Vis alle\") and\n  tax_deduction_ssn_suspicious_message (was \"Kontroller venligst at det er\n  korrekt.\"), and wire both through the types and components. The latter also\n  had to be added to DonorPane''s explicit text allow-list in Widget.tsx.\n- Populate NO/DK/SE datasets with localized ui_labels, operations copy,\n  cause-area selection copy and smart-distribution titles via a new idempotent\n  Sanity CLI script (studio/scripts/localizeWidgetTexts.ts). It only fills\n  missing fields, so hand-authored copy is never clobbered. This is what fixes\n  the SE summary showing the English \"Operations\" instead of \"Drift\".\n\nCause area IDs are assigned per platform and differ between Gi/Giv/Ge Effektivt,\nso the hardcoded ID 4 (operations) and ID 5 (other) were wrong off Sweden -\nneither exists in Norway or Denmark:\n\n- operations_cause_area_id is now optional end to end (undefined = platform has\n  no dedicated operations cause area) instead of silently defaulting to 4, and\n  the summary only renders an operations line when one is configured.\n- donationCalculations no longer hardcodes `area.id === 5`; it uses the\n  configured excluded-cause-area list, which the same function already\n  consulted elsewhere.\n- Drop the ID-bearing defaults from widgetDefaults - a cross-platform default\n  cause area ID can only ever point at the wrong thing.\n- Add CauseAreaSelectInput/CauseAreaMultiSelectInput studio components that\n  read the live cause areas from each platform''s own API, so editors pick real\n  cause areas by name instead of typing raw IDs. They warn about IDs that don''t\n  exist on the platform and fall back to numeric entry if the API is down.\n\nDK e2e now runs as a three-cause-area platform (Global sundhed, Dyrevelfærd,\nDrift) per review feedback, with a Smart fordeling organization at 100% standard\nshare in both Global sundhed and Dyrevelfærd, mirroring how DK really models it.\nwidget.js navigates the cause-area selection step accordingly, and the trailing\nnext-button press is gone because the multi-cause-area donor pane submits\nstraight from the payment tile.","tree":{"sha":"714f72313a4d0d16019a4040e3bc3a2bb81476ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/trees/714f72313a4d0d16019a4040e3bc3a2bb81476ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/git/commits/8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25","node_id":"C_kwDOGueVwtoAKDhmMGE5MWE4NDc5NWJmZGQzODg3MzhjMDliY2QzYTcwYTAwODdmMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commit/32d53354427e765720f01ff084223cf8ba00029f","sha":"32d53354427e765720f01ff084223cf8ba00029f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/32d53354427e765720f01ff084223cf8ba00029f"}],"sha":"8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits/8f0a91a84795bfdd388738c09bcd3a70a0087f25"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/stiftelsen-effekt/main-site/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=bb5e234902534fff38268a701de18c970f7c6d84&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T15%3A44%3A21.136Z"}');
